    backlog:hasTestSpec "Deck of the Threads subject (file slot 25), 26 slides, notes 26/26 (re-read by the lineage session with python-pptx). Reported by the building agent: structure 0 paragraphs PowerPoint would repair; deck_check 19 console rows, 2 charts and 4 tables recomputed, 0 mismatches; program_check 17 panels each run twice with equal transcripts, exit 0 (run under system python3 with the 3.14.6 interpreter, because the check now fails when Pillow is missing); 5 pictures (4 photographs against photos/, 1 program-saved) 0 mismatches; diagram_check 7/7 diagrams, 76 labels verbatim; layout clean; fit 357 frames 0 overflow 0 overlap; notes PASS; honesty_check 17 programs, 2 stand-in slides, 4 NOT EXECUTED, 7 Recorded, 0 refusals; links_check 13/13 HTTP 200; all 20 stale fixtures refused by the check that owns them; re-encoded picture and photograph controls accepted. NOT EXECUTED slides 11, 18, 20, 23 (real xkcd.com, free-threaded 3.13, C extension re-enabling the GIL, Windows/macOS, more than 2 CPUs, runs under load). Recorded slides 4, 9, 18, 19, 20, 21, 23; local stand-in server on slides 10 and 11. Stated deviations: program_check and honesty_check extended to cover photographs (stricter, not weaker); two programs have lines over 67 characters (the book's own 77-character line and a hidden interpreter path line); one research figure is 0.501 in the research and 0.503 in its timing record, the deck uses 0.503; slides 11, 17 and 19 carry shorter explanatory text because panels filled the height. ORDER DISCLOSURE: the builder was launched, and the deck committed, before the start record (v2.128.0) was committed; the start time in the register is when the start was written, not witnessed ahead of the work by git." ;
