ex:Gap_OutScope_Ch07_12 a backlog:PartialScopeDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Out-scoping of the work of this lineage that is not finished"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor ex:Lineage ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:outScopes ex:ST_Deck_Ch07, ex:ST_Research_Ch07, ex:ST_Page_Ch07, ex:ST_Deck_Ch08, ex:ST_Research_Ch08, ex:ST_Page_Ch08, ex:ST_Deck_Ch09, ex:ST_Research_Ch09, ex:ST_Page_Ch09, ex:ST_Deck_Ch10, ex:ST_Research_Ch10, ex:ST_Page_Ch10, ex:ST_Deck_Ch11, ex:ST_Research_Ch11, ex:ST_Page_Ch11, ex:ST_Deck_Ch12, ex:ST_Research_Ch12, ex:ST_Page_Ch12, ex:ST_ReworkOthers_Ch01_02_04, ex:EP_Deck, ex:EP_Research, ex:EP_Page, ex:Init_Slides ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "The deck, research and page stories of chapters 7 to 12 (18 stories) are finished in the course repository but were never planned, started or recorded here: they were built outside this register, and their stories still read Proposed with no planning event. Recording them Done inside this lineage would be backfilling closed work that was never planned (G23, G105). The story for the rework of the decks and pages of chapters 1, 2 and 4 with the teaching devices is held by the owner until he judges chapter 3 mature, which he has not done; it is unfinished. The three epics and the initiative that group the stories are open while any of those stories is open. All of them leave this lineage unchanged and unfinished, so that this lineage closes with no unfinished work inside it; the successor lineage under the same mission takes them in. Decided by the owner on 2026-10-12 (chapters 7 to 12 are tasks completed before the lineage, to be closed appropriately and kept outside the new scope) and executed on the framework ruling of the same date." .

ex:Lineage2 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Second lineage run for the SEN0414 decks: the work finished before it was planned"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 2 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_InProgress ;
    backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 ; backlog:adoptionRecordedAtOpen true .

ex:Succession_Ch07_12 a backlog:LineageSuccession ;
    rdfs:label "Succession that takes in the out-scoped work of chapters 7 to 12"@en ;
    backlog:succeedsLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:successorLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:resolvesGap ex:Gap_OutScope_Ch07_12 ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:successionRationale "The first lineage planned and finished chapters 1 to 6 and 13 to 24 with multithreading, each with a planning event before its work and evidence after it. Chapters 7 to 12 were built, tested and pushed before they were planned, so the first lineage can neither record them Done (that would add planning events after the work and move finished-late items) nor close with them still Proposed (closing unfinished work is not allowed). Restarting it would retract five correct stage outputs and answer a bypass that the order check does not find (it reads ORDERED). The owner therefore out-scoped the unfinished and unrecorded work in the previous event, this lineage closes complete on what it finished, and a successor under the same mission opens with the Scope of admitting the finished chapters, recorded now with their real finish dates from git. Cost of waiting: the register keeps stating Proposed for eighteen finished stories; cost of acting: one succession, five stage commits, and evidence re-run for eighteen items; enforcement value forgone: none, the chain of the first lineage stays untouched." .

