ex:AC2S_Page_Ch06 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page of chapter 6 meets the page standard with the chapter-code tab in the deck's order"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard): the owner asks that the chapter 6 page meet the same standards as the sibling course's chapters 5 and 6, above all that the slide code appears in the same order in a chapter-code tab that runs it. Given the existing page of chapter 6 and the rebuilt deck of chapter 6, when the page is rebuilt as a new file with a new page version on the template 9.52.1 with the builders v4_18_0 and v2_25_0, then ALL of: (1) the page test 9.37.0 runs all its added features with no skip and passes them (P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11), exit 0; (2) the page test 9.34.0 reports no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the existing page, skipped not more; (3) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names, code and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result (measured by the page test); (4) the chapter checks that exist for the chapter (Research, Page) pass; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed beyond the new files; the stored page-test result is a new file; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.37.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_PageTest37, ex:TS2_PageTemplate, ex:TS2_PageBuilder, ex:TS2_PageData, ex:TS2_PageTest34, ex:TS2_ChapterCheck, ex:TS2_RdodiGates ;
