    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T08:50:32"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T11:42:46"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deckcheck, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deckcheck_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deckcheck_1 ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW files 08-tooling/sen0414_deck_standard_check_v1_0_0.py and 08-tooling/sen0414_deck_overlap_check_v1_0_0.py as new-named copies of the sibling's tools (read-only sources: /home/claude/sen0401/08-tooling/sen0401_deck_standard_check_v1_0_0.py and /home/claude/sen0401/08-tooling/deck_overlap_check_v1_0_0.py; only the root, the prefix, the brand mark and the file names change; any other change is stated and justified). One named, exit-coded result per element D1 to D12 for a deck given by chapter number, printing the measured number for each. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. Define each element's measure in the file header (as the sibling's header does). Prove them by running the deck check on the three existing decks (chapter 6: 03-materials/ch06/SEN0414_Ch06_Lists_3e_v2_0_0.pptx; chapter 7: 03-materials/ch07/SEN0414_Ch07_Dictionaries_3e_v1_0_0.pptx; chapter 8: 08-tooling/ch08-deck/sen0414_ch08_deck_v1_0_0.pptx) and the overlap check on the same decks: they must reproduce the measured facts of ex:IA2_Standard (slide counts, code slides, native charts, concept counts, the failing elements) or explain every difference, and settle the discrepancy on D8 of the chapter 8 deck by reading the slide. Keep the logs. Do not judge any deck you build: you build no deck in this iteration. The checks must also measure the code manifest equality (deck code boxes equal the manifest file, text and order) once a manifest exists. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I18-deckcheck; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

