    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_v9_36_0.py from sen0414_page_test_v9_34_0.py (which stays byte-identical), taking the page-standard features from the sibling's page test 9.36.0 (read-only: /home/claude/sen0401/08-tooling/sen0401_page_test_v9_36_0.py): every feature of 9.34.0 stays textually identical; add the features P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9 and P11 of the page standard, which apply to a page that declares the standard (meta page-standard 9.52) and are reported as SKIP with the reason 'page does not declare the standard' otherwise; an environment switch FORCE_STANDARD=1 applies them to any page. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. Show: a unified diff against 9.34.0, and the proof that the set of old feature texts is equal. Baseline: run it with FORCE_STANDARD=1 on the three existing pages (chapters 6, 7 and 8, page v9_28_0, through sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py, the TEST release key) and keep the logs: the failing features must name the measured defects (no chapter-code tab, no panel level, no declared standard, and whatever else the run finds). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I18-pagetest; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

