ex:AC2C_Charset a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The new template and the new page test place and check the character-set declaration below byte 512"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed repair (ex:CR2_Charset). Given the page template 9.50.0 (declaration at byte 15897), the sibling's 9.52.1 (byte 13587) and the shipped pages v9_28_0 (byte 9293), when the NEW template 9.52.1 and the NEW page test 9.36.0 are made, then ALL of: (1) the first <meta charset> in the new template 9.52.1 begins below byte 512 and is the first child of <head>; (2) a page of chapter 1 and one of chapter 10 built on it by the new builders also begin the declaration below byte 512; (3) the page test 9.36.0 has the named feature P12, which fails on the shipped pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 (byte 9293) and passes on the built ones, with the raw bytes read; (4) no committed file is edited; results as printed, measured by the controller (the lineage agent) from the files, not from the executors' reports. CHARSET RULE (added to the page standard by this change): the page declares <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> as the FIRST child of <head>, so that its first byte lies below byte 1,024 of the file (the sibling's evidence needs the declaration within the first 1,024 bytes; the lineage's check requires it within the first 512). The template 9.52.1 places it first in head, before any comment, style or script; the builders keep it there; the page test 9.36.0 has a named feature P12 that reads the raw bytes of the built page (not the DOM) and fails when the declaration is absent or begins at or beyond byte 512; FORCE_STANDARD=1 and the declared standard both apply it, and it is never reported as SKIP for a page built from the new template." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_PageTemplate, ex:TS2_PageTest36, ex:TS2_PageBuilder ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0; byte offset read by the controller with python3 (raw bytes of the file)" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the template 9.52.1 and the page test 9.36.0 cited by SHA-256, the byte offsets printed by the controller, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2C_Passes, ex:TC2C_NotClaimed .
ex:TC2C_Passes a backlog:TestCase ; rdfs:label "Read the raw bytes of the built pages and of the template and require the declaration below byte 512"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:exercisesCriterion ex:AC2C_Charset ; backlog:coversScenario ex:Scen2S_P_Passes ; backlog:runsOnData ex:Data2C_Passing ;
    backlog:hasCaseText "The controller reads the new template and the built pages as bytes and prints the offset of the first meta charset: below 512 and first in head; page test feature P12 passes." .
ex:TC2C_NotClaimed a backlog:TestCase ; rdfs:label "Run the page test feature on the shipped pages and the old template and require that it fails"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:exercisesCriterion ex:AC2C_Charset ; backlog:coversScenario ex:Scen2S_P_NotClaimed ; backlog:runsOnData ex:Data2C_Failing ;
    backlog:hasCaseText "Feature P12 of page test 9.36.0 on the shipped pages v9_28_0 (byte 9293) and on the template 9.50.0 (byte 15897) reports FAIL." .
ex:Data2C_Passing a backlog:TestData ; rdfs:label "The new template and pages built from it, declaration first in head"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasFixtureState "Template 9.52.1 and the scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 built on it, whose first meta charset begins below byte 512." .
ex:Data2C_Failing a backlog:TestData ; rdfs:label "The shipped pages and the old template, declaration beyond byte 1024"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasFixtureState "The pages v9_28_0 of chapters 6, 7 and 8 (byte 9293) and the template 9.50.0 (byte 15897)." .

ex:ST_Std_Charset a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Repair: the character-set declaration of the page template and pages is first in head, below byte 512, and the page test checks it"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_Std_Charset" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Repair: the character-set declaration is first in head and checked"  ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Maintenance ;
    backlog:asRole "SEN0414 instructor" ; backlog:wantsCapability "pages whose text shows correctly in every viewer, also those that read only the first 1,024 bytes" ; backlog:soThat "the Turkish and technical characters of the chapter pages are never shown as mojibake" ;
    backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del2_StdTools ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj2_StdPages ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC2C_Charset ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T09:07:13"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T11:42:46"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T19:48:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score7_ST_Std_Charset ; backlog:standsAlone true ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner's standing instruction of Friday 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul (08:07 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" When a repair or defect story enters the backlog, the open items are re-scored with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs stated from observable facts), the new ranking is recorded as dated records, starts are ordered by it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks or that would ship the same defect. Known case to apply now: the SEN0401 sibling found that its page template placed the character-set declaration at byte ~13,600 (beyond the first 1,024 bytes), so pages show mojibake in prescan-only viewers; the SEN0414 template line and its pages 9.28.0 are to be checked for the same fault, a page task that would ship it is ranked behind the template task that places the declaration first in head, and the page test must check it. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; byte offset of the first <meta charset=...> in the file): template 9.48.0 byte 13469, 9.49.0 byte 14037, 9.50.0 byte 15897 (the template line the new template 9.52.1 is ported over); the sibling's template 9.52.1 byte 13587 (head opens at byte 383), so porting the sibling's file would ship the fault; the shipped pages sen0414_ch06_page_v9_28_0.html, ch07 and ch08: byte 9293 each (head opens at byte 31). The page test 9.34.0 of this line has no check of the declaration (no occurrence of charset in the file). The HTML standard's encoding sniffing reads only the first 1,024 bytes for a declaration, so a declaration after that is not seen by a prescan-only viewer. The same holds for the shipped pages of the other chapters built from the same template; they are outside this iteration and are reported, not changed. CHARSET RULE (added to the page standard by this change): the page declares <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> as the FIRST child of <head>, so that its first byte lies below byte 1,024 of the file (the sibling's evidence needs the declaration within the first 1,024 bytes; the lineage's check requires it within the first 512). The template 9.52.1 places it first in head, before any comment, style or script; the builders keep it there; the page test 9.36.0 has a named feature P12 that reads the raw bytes of the built page (not the DOM) and fails when the declaration is absent or begins at or beyond byte 512; FORCE_STANDARD=1 and the declared standard both apply it, and it is never reported as SKIP for a page built from the new template." .

ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Control the character-set repair: byte offsets of the new template and the built pages and the page test feature P12"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_Charset_Verify" ; backlog:hasTitle "Control the character-set repair" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Compliance ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T09:07:13"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T11:42:46"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_charset, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_charset_0 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Template, ex:TK_Std_PageTest ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's score; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Controller task (the lineage agent): after the template 9.52.1 and the page test 9.36.0 are Done, read the raw bytes of the template and of the pages of chapters 1 and 10 built on it and print the offset of the first meta charset (below 512, first child of head); run page test feature P12 on the shipped pages v9_28_0 (must FAIL) and on the built pages (must PASS). Planned session SEN0414-lineage (control); estimated start after the template and the page test, about 1 hour (estimate, G120). CHARSET RULE (added to the page standard by this change): the page declares <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> as the FIRST child of <head>, so that its first byte lies below byte 1,024 of the file (the sibling's evidence needs the declaration within the first 1,024 bytes; the lineage's check requires it within the first 512). The template 9.52.1 places it first in head, before any comment, style or script; the builders keep it there; the page test 9.36.0 has a named feature P12 that reads the raw bytes of the built page (not the DOM) and fails when the declaration is absent or begins at or beyond byte 512; FORCE_STANDARD=1 and the declared standard both apply it, and it is never reported as SKIP for a page built from the new template." .
ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch06_Build backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify .
ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch07_Build backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify .
ex:TK_Std_Page_Ch08_Build backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify .
ex:TK_Std_Template backlog:hasAuditNote "REPAIR REQUIREMENT (ex:CR2_Charset, owner's standing instruction of 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul): the template 9.50.0 and the sibling's 9.52.1 place the character-set declaration at byte 15897 and 13587; the NEW template 9.52.1 must place <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> as the first child of <head>, before any comment, style or script, below byte 512, and the builders must keep it there. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; byte offset of the first <meta charset=...> in the file): template 9.48.0 byte 13469, 9.49.0 byte 14037, 9.50.0 byte 15897 (the template line the new template 9.52.1 is ported over); the sibling's template 9.52.1 byte 13587 (head opens at byte 383), so porting the sibling's file would ship the fault; the shipped pages sen0414_ch06_page_v9_28_0.html, ch07 and ch08: byte 9293 each (head opens at byte 31). The page test 9.34.0 of this line has no check of the declaration (no occurrence of charset in the file). The HTML standard's encoding sniffing reads only the first 1,024 bytes for a declaration, so a declaration after that is not seen by a prescan-only viewer. The same holds for the shipped pages of the other chapters built from the same template; they are outside this iteration and are reported, not changed." .
ex:TK_Std_PageTest backlog:hasAuditNote "REPAIR REQUIREMENT (ex:CR2_Charset, owner's standing instruction of 2026-10-23 11:07 Istanbul): add the named feature P12 to the NEW page test 9.36.0: it reads the raw bytes of the built page (not the DOM) and fails when no <meta charset> is present or its first byte lies at or beyond byte 512; it is applied to every page built from the new template, with the declared standard or FORCE_STANDARD=1, and is reported SKIP only for a page that does not declare the standard; prove it fails on the shipped pages (v9_28_0, byte 9293) and on a copy of the template 9.50.0 and passes on a page with the declaration first in head. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, read-only, 2026-10-23; byte offset of the first <meta charset=...> in the file): template 9.48.0 byte 13469, 9.49.0 byte 14037, 9.50.0 byte 15897 (the template line the new template 9.52.1 is ported over); the sibling's template 9.52.1 byte 13587 (head opens at byte 383), so porting the sibling's file would ship the fault; the shipped pages sen0414_ch06_page_v9_28_0.html, ch07 and ch08: byte 9293 each (head opens at byte 31). The page test 9.34.0 of this line has no check of the declaration (no occurrence of charset in the file). The HTML standard's encoding sniffing reads only the first 1,024 bytes for a declaration, so a declaration after that is not seen by a prescan-only viewer. The same holds for the shipped pages of the other chapters built from the same template; they are outside this iteration and are reported, not changed." .
