    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T12:43:39"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T16:25:56"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T19:48:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score7_ST_Std_TemplateFix ; backlog:standsAlone true ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner's standing rule (2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed): \"Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks.\" A repair entering the backlog re-ranks the open items with the register's own ranking discipline (PriorityScore, inputs from observable facts), the ranking is recorded as dated records, starts follow it, and a repair outranks the work it blocks. The course coordinator's direction of the same day: run the change route for both findings now, put the template repair (a new template version with its own check) and the runner repair ahead of the page builds, re-score dated, release the page builds only after the repairs are controlled; the owner is in class and needs the pages as soon as possible. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-23, Playwright 1.56.0, Chromium, 1400x900; repeatable). FINDING 1, the template: pages built on template 9.52.1 fail two features that 9.34.0 owns and that the shipped pages v9_28_0 and pages built on 9.50.0 from the same page data pass: 'a focused concept starts at the top' (first paragraph 410 px from the top, limit 240; 9.50.0: 210 px) and 'small phone (360px)' (the explorer-drawer check). ROOT CAUSE: the description comment at the head of course_page_template_v9_52_1.html (text carried over from the sibling's 9.52.0 and 9.52.1 descriptions) contains two literal '-->' sequences (36 comment closers against 34 openers); the first closes the comment at byte 1157, so about 1,157 characters of description prose are rendered as visible text of the page body above the header: the header starts at 190 px instead of 0, every concept sits 200 px lower, and at 360 px the layout of the drawer check changes. The comment of 9.50.0 is balanced (33 and 33). The character-set rule is not affected (the declaration stays at byte 37). The executor's own chapter 10 log shows both features passing; the lineage agent re-ran the executor's own scratch page file with its own driver and got FAIL on both, so the difference lies in what the executor's run measured, not in the file (the repair task must state why). FINDING 2, the runner: 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_run_v1_0_0.py names sen0414_page_test_v9_34_0.py in its code (line 24); a run through it never executes the features P1 to P12 of 9.36.0." .

