    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T12:43:39"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T16:25:56"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_templatefix, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_templatefix_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_templatefix_1 ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW files 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_2.html (from course_page_template_v9_52_1.html, which stays byte-identical) and 08-tooling/sen0414_page_build_v4_18_1.py (from sen0414_page_build_v4_18_0.py, byte-identical). ROOT CAUSE measured by the lineage agent (repeat it first and print it): the description comment at the head of 9.52.1 contains two literal '-->' sequences (36 closers against 34 openers; the first closes the comment at byte 1157), so about 1,157 characters of description prose are visible text above the header: header at 190 px instead of 0, first paragraph at 410 px instead of 210 on the same data. Repair: rewrite the comment so no '-->' lies inside it (keep the version history as text), keep everything else of 9.52.1 as it is (charset first in head below byte 512, ids, hooks, behaviour). The builder 4.18.1 differs from 4.18.0 only by the default template 9.52.2 and a guard: it refuses a template whose comment openers and closers differ in number or whose text between <body> and the header is not empty, and keeps the charset guard. Prove: (a) build scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 on 9.52.2 (PAGE_SCRATCH and PAGE_DATA_DIR outside the repository; take the page data from the data builder 2.25.0 as before) and show the header at 0 px and no body text before it; (b) show that the guard refuses 9.52.1; (c) run the page tests 9.34.0 and 9.36.0 on both pages, one at a time, with the TEST key (your own key-substituting driver), and keep the logs: no [FAIL] line; (d) STATE WHY your earlier log of 9.52.1 on chapter 10 showed 'a focused concept starts at the top' and 'small phone' passing while the lineage agent's re-run of your page file failed: build the page again, compare it with the page you tested, and print the difference. Do not use the new runner or any file of the runner repair. Do not edit any committed file. Planned session SEN0414-I18-template-r2; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

