ex:CR2_Priority3 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Owner priority decision: chapters 7, 8 and 9 first for next week, chapter 6 behind them; then all chapters retrofitted from chapter 1, then the remaining chapters built"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "OWNER DECISION of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation), a priority input: SEN0414 chapters 7, 8 and 9 are urgent for next week; chapter 6 drops behind them. After they are finished, return to ALL chapters starting with chapter 1 (retrofit to the standard: deck, chapter-code manifest, page), and after that build all remaining chapters. The coordinator's direction: add chapter 9 (deck, manifest, page) to Iter_18; check what exists for chapter 9; re-rank dated (chapters 7, 8, 9 deck and page ahead of the chapter 6 page, the repairs still first); plan the follow-on as planned work with estimates, not started now. The owner's standing rule that repairs re-rank the open items also holds. The scope grows by chapter 9 (deck, manifest, page), which the exclusion ex:Excl2_NoRebuild still holds out, and by planned, not started, work for the other chapters. Pending until the ScopeChange that records it." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_Priority3 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the owner priority decision changes: chapter 9 enters Iter_18, the open stories are re-ranked, the follow-on is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Priority3 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-23, from the repository). CHAPTER 9 (Regular Expressions): research exists (03-materials/ch09/rdodi: document v1_0_0 and v1_0_1, domain TBox, ABox and SHACL, research v1_0_0); an old deck exists only as 08-tooling/ch09-deck/sen0414_ch09_deck_v1_0_0.pptx with its generator, examples and checks (03-materials/ch09 holds no deck); the old page exists as 03-materials/ch09/page/sen0414_ch09_page_v9_28_0.html (and 9_17_0, 9_18_0, 9_19_0): no chapter-code tab, no panel level, no declared standard, the character-set declaration at byte 9293; no chapter-code manifest exists. So chapter 9 needs a new deck (as a new file in 03-materials/ch09), its chapter-code manifest, then a new page, exactly as chapters 6, 7 and 8. OTHER CHAPTERS: chapters 1 to 5 and 10 to 24 have research, an old deck and an old page of the same kind (chapter 25, threads, has research, one deck file and one page file); none has a chapter-code manifest. ESTIMATES (the register's own, from the controlled chapters 6 to 8 of this iteration: a deck rebuild about 5.0 h of one executor session, a page rebuild about 4.0 h, the controller's control about 1.0 h per chapter): a retrofit of one chapter is about 10.0 h of work, about 9.0 h of it by executors; the 21 chapters 1 to 5 and 10 to 25 are about 210 h in all, about 70 h of wall time with three executor sessions in parallel (a deck session, a page session, a second chapter's deck session; the 2-core machine and the controller's control are the limit). Chapters still lacking research, deck or page after the retrofits are built from scratch at about 12.0 h each (research 3.0 h, deck 5.0 h, page 4.0 h); their list is measured when the retrofits finish. Ranking after the owner decision (WSJF, inputs from observable facts): the repairs still rank first (a repair outranks the work it blocks); then the chapter 7, 8 and 9 pages (time criticality 20: next week), the chapter 9 deck first because the chapter 9 page depends on it; the chapter 6 page drops to time criticality 8. The deck of chapter 9 is a prerequisite and starts at once, in parallel with the repairs, although its own score is below the pages' (a dependency orders starts before a score does). WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage is revised once more (stories, criteria and tasks added; the digest moves); tasks already Done stay Done and are not re-dated; the two repair tasks already begun are not touched; the page builds keep their dependencies on the repairs' verification; the follow-on stories are planned and unscored (scored when their iteration is planned), start nothing, and are admitted only as planned work. Not in the plan: any edit of a committed file." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog4 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the owner priority decision of 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_Priority3, ex:IA2_Priority3 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "OWNER DECISION of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded as relayed (content, not a verbatim quotation), a priority input: SEN0414 chapters 7, 8 and 9 are urgent for next week; chapter 6 drops behind them. After they are finished, return to ALL chapters starting with chapter 1 (retrofit to the standard: deck, chapter-code manifest, page), and after that build all remaining chapters. The coordinator's direction: add chapter 9 (deck, manifest, page) to Iter_18; check what exists for chapter 9; re-rank dated (chapters 7, 8, 9 deck and page ahead of the chapter 6 page, the repairs still first); plan the follow-on as planned work with estimates, not started now. The owner's standing rule that repairs re-rank the open items also holds. Stories, criteria and tasks are added to the closed Backlog stage, which moves its digest (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage; the change request ex:CR2_Priority3 and the impact assessment ex:IA2_Priority3 were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR3 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR4 and re-admits every item without re-dating it; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output stays as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "6b88701680346d52b1f6bded8aa68f1141116ad2" .
