ex:AC2S_Deck_Ch09 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck of chapter 9 meets every element of the deck standard, with its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard): the owner asks that the chapter 9 deck meet the same standards as the sibling course's chapters 5 and 6. Given the existing deck of chapter 9 and its research, when the deck is rebuilt as a new file with a new version number and its chapter-code manifest written, then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check v1_0_0 for chapter 9 reports every element D1 to D12 met and exits 0; (2) the deck overlap check v1_0_0 reports no overlap; (3) the chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch09_v1_0_0.json lists the deck's code examples in slide order, by name, and its code and order equal the deck's code boxes (measured by the deck check); (4) the chapter's own build checks that exist for it pass (the chapter check v1_1_0 Deck/Ch09 where it covers the chapter); (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_ChapterCheck ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2S_D_Passes, ex:TC2S_D_NotClaimed .

ex:AC2S_Page_Ch09 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page of chapter 9 meets the page standard with the chapter-code tab in the deck's order"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR2_Standard): the owner asks that the chapter 9 page meet the same standards as the sibling course's chapters 5 and 6, above all that the slide code appears in the same order in a chapter-code tab that runs it. Given the existing page of chapter 9 and the rebuilt deck of chapter 9, when the page is rebuilt as a new file with a new page version on the template 9.52.1 with the builders v4_18_0 and v2_25_0, then ALL of: (1) the page test 9.37.0 runs all its added features with no skip and passes them (P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11), exit 0; (2) the page test 9.34.0 reports no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the existing page, skipped not more; (3) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names, code and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result (measured by the page test); (4) the chapter checks that exist for the chapter (Research, Page) pass; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed beyond the new files; the stored page-test result is a new file; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.37.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_PageTest37, ex:TS2_PageTemplate, ex:TS2_PageBuilder, ex:TS2_PageData, ex:TS2_PageTest34, ex:TS2_ChapterCheck, ex:TS2_RdodiGates ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.37.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
