ex:AC2R_PageTest37 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The corrected page test 9.37.0 waits for the finished result of a chapter-code example and judges an expected error message by the recorded result, and every other feature is unchanged"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed repair (ex:CR2_Retest37). Given the page test 9.36.0 (it reads a chapter-code result while the placeholder 'Running...' is shown, and flags an example whose recorded expected result is itself an error message), when the NEW file 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py is made from 9.36.0, then ALL of: (1) the file is new and 9.36.0 and 9.34.0 are byte-identical; (2) the ONLY differences from 9.36.0 are: the version line and a comment naming this change; the wait in the P2 chapter-code step, which after Run waits until the result element no longer shows the placeholder 'Running...' (three dots or the ellipsis character) and holds text or a visual, same 90 s bound; and the error check of that step, which flags 'Traceback', 'NameError' or 'Error:' in a result only when the same text is NOT part of the example's recorded expected result in the manifest; every other feature, threshold and message is that of 9.36.0 (a diff proves it); (3) run through the runner v1_1_0 with PAGE_TEST_FILE=sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py, the page of chapter 7 v9_90_0 and the page of chapter 8 v9_90_0 end exit 0 with no failed feature and the same widgets and features as under 9.36.0, and the page of chapter 6 v9_90_0 ends exit 0 with no failed feature (examples 2 and 24 now read their final results); (4) four fixtures (scratch pages or manifests outside the repository) prove the check: a result that stays text-only fails; a real crash (a Python error that is NOT in the example's recorded expected result) fails; a slow visual (result shown after the placeholder, later than 0.5 s) passes; an example whose recorded expected result is itself an error message and whose page shows it passes; (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed, measured by the controller from the files and by its own page-test runs, serially under the shared lock." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_PageTest37, ex:TS2_PageTest36, ex:TS2_PageTest34 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0; page test 9.37.0 (new file over 9.36.0), 9.36.0 and 9.34.0 (Playwright 1.56.0); runner 1.1.0 with PAGE_TEST_FILE" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new file cited by SHA-256, the logs of the controller's own runs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2T_Passes, ex:TC2T_NotClaimed .

ex:ST_Std_PageTest37 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Repair: the page test waits for the finished result of a chapter-code example and judges an expected error message by the recorded result"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_Std_PageTest37" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Repair: the page test waits for the finished result of a chapter-code example and judges an expected error message by the recorded result" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Maintenance ;
    backlog:asRole "SEN0414 instructor" ; backlog:wantsCapability "a page test that does not fail a page for reading a result too early or for an error message the book itself shows" ; backlog:soThat "the chapter pages are measured on the finished result of every example, not on the placeholder" ;
    backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del2_StdTools ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj2_StdPages ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC2R_PageTest37 ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_Std_PageTest37, ex:TK_Std_PageTest37_Verify ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T20:41:49"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-24T23:54:34"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-25T01:12:14"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score15_ST_Std_PageTest37 ; backlog:standsAlone true ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the known race in page test 9.36.0 (the chapter-code step reads an example's result while it still shows 'Running...') may hit the SEN0414 pages; the sibling course restated its page criteria on a corrected test 9.37.0; decide by the change route, without waiting for the owner, whether the chapter 6 and chapter 9 page criteria should name a corrected SEN0414 test, only if the executors actually hit it; disclose in one line. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with also holds. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-24, Playwright 1.56.0, Chromium 1366x768): the executor of the chapter 6 page ran the page test 9.36.0 on its page (commit ff8dedf, log 08-tooling/ch06-page/logs_iter18/page_test_9_36_0_run1.log): exit with the feature 'P2 every chapter-code example opens in the editor, runs in the page ... and shows a visualised result' FAILING with 2 defects out of 24 examples: '2 Lists of lists and a wrong index' and '24 Coin Flip Streaks: result is text, not a visualisation'. The lineage agent's own probe of the same page (first example of a session: the page loads Python on the first run, 3.7 s) shows the cause of both: the test waits only until the result element holds ANY text (line 1597 of sen0414_page_test_v9_36_0.py: textContent length above 0 or an svg/canvas/img/table) and then reads after 300 ms; the page writes the placeholder 'Running...' into that element when Run is clicked, so a result slower than about 0.5 s is read as the text 'Running...' with no visual (examples 2 and 24 read exactly that: {t: 'Running...', v: false}); once the placeholder is gone the same examples show 'code -> Python -> lines in a result card (3716 ms and 622 ms) same result as on the slide' with the visual present. The second cause is separate: the test flags a result whose first 160 characters contain 'Error:' (line 1600), and chapter 6 example 2 is the book's IndexError demonstration, whose recorded expected result in the deck's manifest ends 'IndexError: list index out of range' and which the page reproduces ('same result as on the slide'); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 passed because their error demonstrations print the error name without a colon. The sibling's corrected file (/home/claude/sen0401/08-tooling/sen0401_page_test_v9_37_0.py, controlled in its register) changes only the wait for the placeholder; it does not touch the second cause. Pages that passed 9.36.0 (chapters 7 and 8) are unchanged and stay valid." .

ex:TK_Std_PageTest37 a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make the page test 9.37.0: wait for the finished result and judge an expected error message by the recorded result"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Std_PageTest37" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make the page test 9.37.0: wait for the finished result and judge an expected error message by the recorded result" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T20:41:49"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-24T23:54:34"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_pagetest37, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_pagetest37_0 ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py from sen0414_page_test_v9_36_0.py (which stays byte-identical; read it first). Change ONLY: (a) __version__ = \"9.37.0\" and a comment line naming this change (ex:CR2_Retest37); (b) in the P2 chapter-code run step (the loop over CCI that clicks [data-cc-run], about line 1597), replace the wait with one that returns true when the result element [data-cc-result] exists, its trimmed text is NOT the placeholder matched by /^Running(\\.\\.\\.|\\u2026)$/ and it holds text or an svg/canvas/img/table (same 90000 ms bound), keep the 300 ms pause and the read; (c) in the same step, flag a result for 'Traceback|NameError|Error:' only when the matched text does not occur in the example's recorded expected result (CCI[i] carries the manifest example; use its 'expected' field, normalised for whitespace) - an example whose expected result is itself an error message, such as chapter 6 example 2, is then judged by its visual and by 'same result as on the slide' like any other. The sibling's file /home/claude/sen0401/08-tooling/sen0401_page_test_v9_37_0.py shows change (b) (read-only source, never edited; its first line of the diff against its 9.36.0 is the guide). Prove: (1) the diff of your file against 9.36.0 shows exactly (a), (b), (c); (2) run it through the runner sen0414_page_test_run_v1_1_0.py with PAGE_TEST_FILE=sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py on the pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 v9_90_0, one run at a time under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, and keep every log; (3) build four fixtures outside the repository (text-only result, real crash, slow visual after 1.5 s, expected error message equal to the recorded result) and show: text-only fails, crash fails, slow visual passes, expected error passes, each with its log; (4) do not edit any committed file; report the commit SHAs, the new files and the verbatim output of every run, and say what failed if anything. Planned session SEN0414-I18-pagetest37; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 0.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

