    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the executor of the chapter 6 page reports that the chapter check Research/Ch06 fails on the research v2_0_0 and asks whether this belongs to the page criterion or is a separate gap; proceed at once with the research repair by the change route, a new research data version with its own story ranked before the verify task of the chapter 6 page. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with, and that gaps are said openly, also holds. The scope does not move outward in deliverables: the chapter 6 research is a file of the chapter the pages criterion already names (element 4); what is added is one repair story with a build task and a controller task." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_ResFix06 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the repair of the chapter 6 research changes in the iteration, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_ResFix06 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the executor of the chapter 6 page, log 08-tooling/ch06-page/logs_iter18/chapter_check_Research_Ch06_run1.log, commit ae0ba44; the lineage agent read the log and the files on 2026-10-24): the chapter check Research/Ch06 ends 'RESULT Research/Ch06: FAIL' on the chapter 6 research v2_0_0 (08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_0_0.py, committed 98c1609, 2026-09). The gates (sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py) end 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage4.cov 'hollow instantiation: 11 typed individuals lack label+content' and Stage4.sub '152 individuals not substantive (e.g. s_MembershipOperators: 2 words (<5))'; HermiT is consistent. The execution checks (sen0414_rdodi_checks_v1_2_0.py on sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_0_0) end with 77 checks and 2 mismatches: the class list of the TBox and the individual list of the ABox of the data module differ from the ones the checks expect. The chapter checks of chapters 7 and 8 pass. The failure is therefore not caused by the page work: it is a gap of the chapter 6 research that existed before iteration 18 (the chapter check covered chapters 7 to 12 only until its version 1_1_0 of this iteration reached chapter 6); it belongs to the criterion element (4) of the page criterion ('the chapter checks that exist for the chapter pass'), which is why the chapter 6 page cannot be Done on it, and it is repaired in its own story, not waived. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage of the second lineage is revised once more (a story, a criterion, test cases and two tasks are added; the exclusion on rebuilding is lifted for the NEW research files of chapter 6 only; the digest moves); the tasks already Done stay Done and are not re-dated; the verify task of the chapter 6 page gains the dependency on the controller task of this repair, so the chapter 6 page cannot be Done before the research check passes; the chapter 6 page build task is not blocked; the pages of chapters 7, 8 and 9 and the chapter 9 research are not affected; the open stories are re-scored. Not in the plan: any edit of a committed file, any change of a gate or check, any waiver." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog6 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the repair of the chapter 6 research"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_ResFix06, ex:IA2_ResFix06 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the executor of the chapter 6 page reports that the chapter check Research/Ch06 fails on the research v2_0_0 and asks whether this belongs to the page criterion or is a separate gap; proceed at once with the research repair by the change route, a new research data version with its own story ranked before the verify task of the chapter 6 page. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with, and that gaps are said openly, also holds. A story, a criterion and tasks are added to the lineage's closed Backlog stage and one dependency and one exclusion note are added, which moves its digest (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request ex:CR2_ResFix06 and the impact assessment ex:IA2_ResFix06 were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR5 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR6 and re-admits every item, the Done tasks included, without re-dating them; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR5 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "bec9039" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR5 backlog:outputRetracted true .

