ex:AC2R_ResearchCh06 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The chapter 6 research passes the chapter check Research/Ch06 on a new data version, and the chapter checks of the other chapters still pass"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed repair (ex:CR2_ResFix06 widened by ex:CR2_ResFix06B, restated by ex:CR2_ResFix06C). Given the chapter 6 research set (data module v2_0_0, page ABox v1_3_0: gates Stage4.cov 11 hollow typed individuals, Stage4.sub 152 individuals not substantive; execution checks: 2 mismatches), when (A) a NEW data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_1_0.py is written from v2_0_0 with TAX and BODY taken from the chapter corpus sen0414_ch06_corpus_v1_0_0.py as chapter 7 v1_3_0 did, and the chapter 6 files are rebuilt from it by the generic builder (sen0414_rdodi_build_v1_2_0.py) as 03-materials/ch06/rdodi/sen0414_ch06_{document,domain_tbox,domain_abox,domain_shacl,research}_v2_1_0.*, and (B) a NEW page-ABox builder version 08-tooling/sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_9.py (older versions stay) builds a NEW page ABox 03-materials/ch06/page/sen0414_ch06_page_abox_v1_4_0.ttl that describes the NEW page 03-materials/ch06/page/sen0414_ch06_page_v9_90_0.html (its menus, tabs, panels, widgets and the chapter-code examples as they are in that page), then ALL of: (1) every new file is new and every committed file (the v2_0_0 and v1_0_0 research files, page ABox v1_3_0, the page, the deck, the manifest, the older builders) is byte-identical; (2) every typed individual of the new research ABox and of the new page ABox has a label, a skos:definition and a dcterms:source where the gates ask for them, and content of at least five words that is substantive by the gate, written from the book's chapter 6, the deck, the page and the existing content, with nothing invented; no individual, class, link or source of the old files is dropped without a stated reason; (3) the chapter check Research/Ch06 (python3 08-tooling/sen0414_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py Research/Ch06) ends exit 0 with 'RESULT Research/Ch06: PASS': the gates 'OVERALL: PASS' with Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src passing on the NEW page ABox, HermiT consistent, the execution checks with 0 mismatches; Cross.B must not FAIL; it reports CANNOT_RUN (0 hybrid chains) and is reported openly as such and NOT counted as a pass (the gap is tracked by the planned story ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB); (4) the chapter 6 deck, page and chapter-code manifest are not changed (the page file keeps its SHA-256), and Page/Ch06 under the chapter check still ends PASS; (5) Research/Ch07, Research/Ch08 and Research/Ch09 still end PASS; no committed file is edited; results as printed, measured by the controller by its own re-runs." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_ChapterCheck, ex:TS2_RdodiGates, ex:TS2_PageAboxBuild ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2); deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0, new file over 9.34.0: every feature of 9.34.0 unchanged, the page-standard features added); page test 9.34.0; page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.50.0); page builder v4_18_0 and page-data builder v2_25_0 (new files over v4_17_0 and v2_24_0); chapter check v1_1_0 of this register; RDODI gates v1_1_1; Playwright 1.56.0; chapter check 1.1.0, RDODI gates 1.1.1, RDODI checks 1.2.0, generic builder 1.2.0, page-ABox builder 1.1.9 (new file over 1.1.8) (Python 3.14, HermiT)" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new data module and the v2_1_0 files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the controller's own runs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2R6_Passes, ex:TC2R6_NotClaimed, ex:TC2R6B_PageAbox .

