    backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score15_ST_Std_ResearchCh06 ; backlog:standsAlone true ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the executor of the chapter 6 page reports that the chapter check Research/Ch06 fails on the research v2_0_0 and asks whether this belongs to the page criterion or is a separate gap; proceed at once with the research repair by the change route, a new research data version with its own story ranked before the verify task of the chapter 6 page. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with, and that gaps are said openly, also holds. MEASURED FACTS (the executor of the chapter 6 page, log 08-tooling/ch06-page/logs_iter18/chapter_check_Research_Ch06_run1.log, commit ae0ba44; the lineage agent read the log and the files on 2026-10-24): the chapter check Research/Ch06 ends 'RESULT Research/Ch06: FAIL' on the chapter 6 research v2_0_0 (08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_0_0.py, committed 98c1609, 2026-09). The gates (sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py) end 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage4.cov 'hollow instantiation: 11 typed individuals lack label+content' and Stage4.sub '152 individuals not substantive (e.g. s_MembershipOperators: 2 words (<5))'; HermiT is consistent. The execution checks (sen0414_rdodi_checks_v1_2_0.py on sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_0_0) end with 77 checks and 2 mismatches: the class list of the TBox and the individual list of the ABox of the data module differ from the ones the checks expect. The chapter checks of chapters 7 and 8 pass. The failure is therefore not caused by the page work: it is a gap of the chapter 6 research that existed before iteration 18 (the chapter check covered chapters 7 to 12 only until its version 1_1_0 of this iteration reached chapter 6); it belongs to the criterion element (4) of the page criterion ('the chapter checks that exist for the chapter pass'), which is why the chapter 6 page cannot be Done on it, and it is repaired in its own story, not waived." .

