    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T21:09:42"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T00:31:21"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_research06, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_research06_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_research06_1, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_research06_2, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_research06_3 ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_1_0.py from sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_0_0.py (read it, its builder 08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_build_v1_2_0.py, the gates sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py and the checks sen0414_rdodi_checks_v1_2_0.py first; the way chapters 7 (v1_3_0) and 8 (v1_0_2) pass them is the guide). Run the chapter check first and read both gate findings and the 2 mismatches of the execution checks: find the root cause of each (the 11 typed individuals without label and content, the 152 individuals whose content has fewer than five words, the TBox class list and ABox individual list the checks expect) and fix them in the data, not in a gate or a check. Content comes from the book's chapter 6 and the existing concept texts; do not invent facts, sources or code. Build the files as v2_1_0 into 03-materials/ch06/rdodi with the generic builder, keep the v2_0_0 files byte-identical, and run: python3 08-tooling/sen0414_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py Research/Ch06 (must end PASS), and Research/Ch07, Research/Ch08, Research/Ch09 (must still end PASS), keeping every log in 08-tooling/ch06-research/logs_iter18/. Do not touch the chapter 6 deck, the page or its manifest. Machine: 2 cores shared; run the Java reasoner checks one at a time. Report the commit SHAs, the new files and the verbatim output of every check, and say what failed if anything. Planned session SEN0414-I18-research-ch06; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

