ex:CR2_ResFix06B a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Widen the repair of the chapter 6 research: the gate findings are measured on the page ABox of chapter 6, so the repair also yields a new page ABox and a new page-ABox builder version"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the executor SEN0414-I18-research-ch06 stopped without changes by the brief's stop condition and found the fact that settles the choice; do not wait for the owner; widen the repair by the change route (option A): the task also produces a NEW page ABox version for chapter 6 built by a new page-ABox builder version, besides the research v2_1_0 data module and files; check that the new page ABox describes the NEW page, and whether chapter 9 has the same exposure. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses is dealt with, that a lineage never waits on unrelated questions, and that gaps are said openly, also holds. The scope does not move outward in deliverables: the page ABox of chapter 6 is a file of the chapter the pages criterion already names (element 4)." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_ResFix06B a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What widening the chapter 6 research repair changes, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_ResFix06B ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the executor's report; the lineage agent read the gates script and the files on 2026-10-24): the gates script 08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_gates_v1_1_1.py runs its Stage 4 on the newest 03-materials/chNN/page/sen0414_chNN_page_abox_v*.ttl when one exists (line 20), and skips Stage 4 when none exists. Chapter 6 has such a page ABox (sen0414_ch06_page_abox_v1_3_0.ttl, committed 0097aae, 2026-09-30, built by sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_7/8); chapters 7, 8 and 9 have none, which is why their Research checks pass. The findings of the executor's run: Stage4.cov 'hollow instantiation: 11 typed individuals lack label+content' = CO1-CO5, Layout, Header, Sidebar, Main, GroupedTopBar, SectionTree (a label but no skos:definition or dcterms:source); Stage4.sub '152 individuals not substantive' = page individuals s_* (58), w_* (57), wv_* (24) and structural ones, each with fewer than five words of content. A research v2_1_0 cannot move these gates. The 2 execution-check mismatches (17 classes missing from the TBox, 11 individuals missing from the ABox) come from the old data module sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_0_0.py (it carries the old v1_0_0 TAX/BODY); chapter 7 v1_3_0 fixed the same kind of drift by taking TAX/BODY from the chapter corpus (sen0414_ch06_corpus_v1_0_0.py). The page ABox of v1_3_0 describes the OLD page (v9_28_0 line); the page of chapter 6 is now v9_90_0 on template 9.52.2, so the NEW page ABox must describe the new page. Chapter 9: the page of chapter 9 v9_90_0 has no page ABox, Stage 4 is skipped and Research/Ch09 passes; it has the same exposure only if a page ABox is ever added for it, which is not planned. The finding is a gap of the chapter 6 research set (research files plus the page ABox) that predates iteration 18; it belongs to element (4) of the chapter 6 page criterion; it is repaired, not waived. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage is revised once more; the criterion of ex:ST_Std_ResearchCh06 is restated (research v2_1_0 plus the new page ABox v1_4_0 and the new builder v1_1_9; the tools list gains the builder); the task ex:TK_Std_ResearchCh06 keeps its start of 2026-10-24T21:09:42 UTC (a T_Start cannot be repeated) and a second executor instance is recorded at the real start of the new session, with a new brief; its job size grows from 3.0 to 6.0 h; the controller task is restated; the open stories are re-scored; the exclusion note is extended to the new page ABox of chapter 6 and its builder (new files only). The verify task of the chapter 6 page keeps its dependency. Not in the plan: any edit of a committed file, a change of a gate or check, a waiver, a change of chapter 9." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog7 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the repair of the chapter 6 research widened to its page ABox"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_ResFix06B, ex:IA2_ResFix06B ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-24, recorded as relayed: the executor SEN0414-I18-research-ch06 stopped without changes by the brief's stop condition and found the fact that settles the choice; do not wait for the owner; widen the repair by the change route (option A): the task also produces a NEW page ABox version for chapter 6 built by a new page-ABox builder version, besides the research v2_1_0 data module and files; check that the new page ABox describes the NEW page, and whether chapter 9 has the same exposure. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses is dealt with, that a lineage never waits on unrelated questions, and that gaps are said openly, also holds. The criterion of a story, a task note and the test cases change, which moves the digest of the lineage's closed Backlog stage (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request ex:CR2_ResFix06B and the impact assessment ex:IA2_ResFix06B were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR6 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR7 and re-admits every item, the Done tasks and the started task included, without re-dating them; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR6 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "c0fda27" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR6 backlog:outputRetracted true .

