    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed: the research repair of chapter 6 is not met by its own account on one point, Cross.B prints CANNOT_RUN while the criterion text says Cross.B passing; decide by the discipline without waiting for the owner: if the criterion text cannot be met by this task and the check has never run for any chapter, record it as a pre-existing gap of the gates, tracked as a work item that the lineage enforces but the work cannot satisfy, and restate the criterion by the change route with disclosure, not silently waived. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with also holds. The scope does not move outward: one planned story is added to the unstarted Iter_19 and two criteria are restated." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_ResFix06C a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What restating the Cross.B element changes, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_ResFix06C ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (executor logs 08-tooling/ch06-research/logs_iter18/gates_ch06_partA_run1.log, gates_ch06_partA_run2.log, gates_ch06_partB_run1.log, chapter_check_Research_Ch06_run1.log, and the controller's own run of the chapter check Research/Ch06 on 2026-10-25): the gates end 'OVERALL: PASS' and print '[CANNOT_RUN ] Cross.B: hybrid chains: 0 checked, 0 broken'; Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS on the new page ABox v1_4_0. Cross.B is evaluated only inside Stage 4, that is only for a chapter that has a page ABox; no chapter had one passing it before (chapters 7 to 9 have none, chapter 6's v1_3_0 failed Stage 4 on other checks), so the check has never produced a measured result in this course. It reports CANNOT_RUN because no hybrid chain (a chain that crosses the research document, the domain ontology and the page ABox) exists in any chapter's files for it to check; building such chains is work on the research design of the course, outside the repair of the findings of ex:CR2_ResFix06 and ex:CR2_ResFix06B. The criterion text this register wrote ('Cross.B passing') is therefore unsatisfiable by the task as it stands; the executor did not fake it and reported it openly. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage is revised once more; element (3) of ex:AC2R_ResearchCh06 is restated (Cross.B must not FAIL; CANNOT_RUN is reported and not counted as a pass); the planned retrofit criterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit names the page test 9.37.0 instead of 9.36.0; one planned story ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB with its criterion enters the unstarted Iter_19, Proposed and unscored; the open stories are re-scored with unchanged inputs. The research repair keeps its tasks and its start; it is controlled after this revision against the restated criterion. Not in the plan: a waiver, an edit of a gate, building hybrid chains now." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog8 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the Cross.B element of the chapter 6 research criterion restated and the gap tracked"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_ResFix06C, ex:IA2_ResFix06C ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed: the research repair of chapter 6 is not met by its own account on one point, Cross.B prints CANNOT_RUN while the criterion text says Cross.B passing; decide by the discipline without waiting for the owner: if the criterion text cannot be met by this task and the check has never run for any chapter, record it as a pre-existing gap of the gates, tracked as a work item that the lineage enforces but the work cannot satisfy, and restate the criterion by the change route with disclosure, not silently waived. The owner's standing rule that work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with also holds. A criterion is restated, a second criterion is restated and a planned story enters the closed Backlog stage, which moves its digest (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request ex:CR2_ResFix06C and the impact assessment ex:IA2_ResFix06C were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR7 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR8 and re-admits every item without re-dating any; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR7 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "19c3dfe" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR7 backlog:outputRetracted true .

