ex:TK_Std_ResearchCh06 backlog:hasAuditNote "CONTROL FINDING of the lineage agent on the executor's second session (commits 0064873, 12b4bd1, f18e3da), NOT MET on element (2) of the criterion, measured on 2026-10-24: the new domain ABox v2_1_0 holds 98 individuals where v2_0_0 holds 105 - seven are missing: the six error-condition individuals Err_Index, Err_IndexMethod, Err_MultipleAssignment, Err_MutableImmutable, Err_RandomChoice, Err_SortMethod (v2_0_0 labels such as '[1, 2, 3][10] raises IndexError: list index out of range') with their rd:hasErrorCondition links, and the third competency question CQ3 (which printed outputs and error messages differ in current Python); the label 'CPython 3.12.3, CPython 3.13.16 and CPython 3.14.6' is also absent. The data module v2_1_0 states that nothing is removed; that statement is wrong, and the execution checks do not see it because the module was made equal to the new ABox, not to v2_0_0. Everything else is met: Research/Ch06 live PASS (Stage4 A, B, cov, sub and src PASS on the new page ABox, HermiT consistent, 86 checks 0 mismatches), Research/Ch07, 08, 09 and Page/Ch06 PASS, no committed file edited (the page test 9.37.0 file of another task excepted and disclosed), the page, manifest and deck unchanged, the new page ABox describes the new page (69 sections, 72 widgets, 24 examples, 8 menus equal the page test counts). Cross.B reports CANNOT_RUN and is not counted as a pass (criterion restated by ex:CR2_ResFix06C; gap tracked by ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB). The task stays InProgress and is NOT Done: the seven individuals are restored in NEW files (data module v2_2_0 and the five ontology files v2_2_0; v2_1_0 is committed and is not edited); the chapter check then runs on v2_2_0 and the controller re-runs it." .


