    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met2_StdDecks ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj2_StdDecks ; backlog:hasObservedValue "3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-10-25T01:12:14"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony ex:RC2_Iter_18B ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Measured in this run (2026-10-25T01:12:14 UTC): the deck standard check v1_0_0 and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 on the newest decks of chapters 6, 7 and 8: chapter 06 passes (SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)); chapter 07 passes (SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)); chapter 08 passes (SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)). The chapter 9 deck (controlled in register 2.177.0) is beyond the metric's three chapters and also passes." .
ex:ObsR2B_Obj2_StdPages a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Reading at the review that closed iteration 18"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met2_StdPages ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj2_StdPages ; backlog:hasObservedValue "3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-10-25T01:12:14"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony ex:RC2_Iter_18B ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Measured in this run (2026-10-25T01:12:14 UTC): the control checks of the pages of chapters 6 (sen0414_control_iter18_v1_6_0.py page06), 7 and 8 (v1_3_0 page07, page08), which re-read the controller's serial page-test runs under the shared lock (9.37.0 and 9.34.0 for chapter 6, 9.36.0 and 9.34.0 for chapters 7 and 8, with the 9.37.0 runs of chapters 7 and 8 giving the same widgets and features), the charset, comments and manifest equality of the newest pages: chapter 06 passes (RESULT PASS (0 failed assertion(s))); chapter 07 passes (RESULT PASS (0 failed assertion(s))); chapter 08 passes (RESULT PASS (0 failed assertion(s))). The restated criteria of the chapter 6 and 9 pages name the page test 9.37.0 (ex:CR2_Retest37); the chapter 9 page is beyond the metric's three chapters and also passes." .
ex:AC2S_Page_Ch06 backlog:hasAuditNote "Tool versions actually used (controlled): the page was built on the template 9.52.2 with the builder 4.18.1 and the page-data builder 2.25.0, read through the runner v1_1_0; the template 9.52.1 and the builder 4.18.0 named in this criterion's text produce a page with text above the header and are superseded by the repair (ex:CR2_Repair2). The page test is 9.37.0 (ex:CR2_Retest37). The criterion's elements were all measured on the page as built; recorded 2026-10-25T01:12:14 UTC at the review." .
ex:AC2S_Page_Ch09 backlog:hasAuditNote "Tool versions actually used (controlled): the page was built on the template 9.52.2 with the builder 4.18.1 and the page-data builder 2.25.0, read through the runner v1_1_0; the template 9.52.1 and the builder 4.18.0 named in this criterion's text produce a page with text above the header and are superseded by the repair (ex:CR2_Repair2). The page test is 9.37.0 (ex:CR2_Retest37). The criterion's elements were all measured on the page as built; recorded 2026-10-25T01:12:14 UTC at the review." .

ex:CR2_Iter19 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Plan Iteration 19: the retrofit of chapters 1 to 5 to the written standard, with the research set of each chapter, and move the later chapters to a new Iteration 20"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed: close the Iteration 18 review, then plan and start the Iteration 19 retrofit from chapter 1 by the change route: re-rank the open items, generate the briefs, give the executor briefs to start; do not wait for the owner. The owner's decision of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC) (ex:CR2_Priority3), recorded as relayed, is the release: after chapters 7, 8 and 9 are finished, return to ALL chapters starting with chapter 1 (retrofit to the standard: deck, chapter-code manifest, page). Chapters 7, 8 and 9 and the repairs are finished and controlled (register 2.201.0). The scope does not move outward: the planned stories of the retrofit were admitted at the owner's decision (ex:CR2_Priority3); this change plans them, adds the tasks, one criterion for the research set and a new unstarted iteration for the later chapters." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_Iter19 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What planning Iteration 19 changes, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Iter19 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25, from the repository; logs 08-tooling/control-iter19-logs/): (1) DECKS: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest deck of each chapter 1 to 5 prints FAILING: chapter 1 fails D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (8 of 13; M1 not measured, no manifest); chapter 2 the same 8; chapter 3 the same 8; chapter 4 the same 8; chapter 5 fails those 8 and D12 (9). Every chapter 1 to 5 has NO chapter-code manifest (03-materials/chNN/page has none) and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 ends FINDINGS on every one (5, 4, 6, 5 and 3 findings for chapters 1 to 5). (2) RESEARCH: the chapter check Research/Ch01 to Research/Ch05 each ends 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage1 to Stage3 PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (hollow typed individuals of the page ABox: 10, 10, 10, 11, 11) and Stage4.sub FAIL (individuals not substantive: 80, 81, 85, 78, 91), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN. It is the defect that chapter 6 had (ex:CR2_ResFix06); for chapters 1 to 5 the research is therefore part of the retrofit, not an extra. (3) THE CHAPTER CHECK does not cover chapters 1 to 5 for Deck and Page: Deck/Ch01 and Deck/Ch02 end in an assertion, Deck/Ch03 and Deck/Ch04 in a missing build script, Deck/Ch05 in StopIteration; Page/Ch01 starts a browser test outside the lock and was stopped. They are the chapters it was never written for (it covers 6 to 12 and chapter 6 partly). The controller measures chapters 1 to 5 with the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the page test 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0, and the chapter check Research/ChNN; adding Deck and Page cases to the chapter check is not part of this plan (a change to a committed tool; a new tool version would be a new item). (4) PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 1 to 5 are v9_28_0 (template 9.50.0, old standard); they have no chapter-code tab. The rebuilt pages follow the pages of chapters 6 to 9 (v9_90_0, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0, page test 9.37.0, runner v1_1_0). (5) PRECEDENT: chapter 9 (deck 2026-10-24 19:37 to 19:58; page 20:05 to 23:54) and chapter 6 (page, then the research repair, which took three executor sessions because the second dropped seven individuals of the old set without saying so: the controller compares the individual sets of the old and new files, and an executor must too). The first story photograph of the chapter 9 page fills the viewport height, so the story text starts below the fold: the retrofit pages must show the story text without scrolling past a full-height photograph (noted at the Iter_18 review). (6) ESTIMATES (G120: estimates, not measurements): deck build 5.0 h, deck verify 0.5 h, page build 3.5 h, research set and page ABox 4.0 h, research verify 0.5 h, page verify 1.0 h: 14.5 h per chapter, 72.5 h for the five; the machine has 2 cores and browser tests run one at a time, so the executor sessions of different chapters overlap only in the deck and research builds. GAPS SAID OPENLY: (a) the metrics Met2_StdDecks and Met2_StdPages count the decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 (target 3) and read 3 and 3 at the Iter_18 review; the retrofit of chapters 1 to 5 moves no number of those metrics, and a metric for it has not been defined: defining one is a change of the Objective stage, held back for the owner's decision on the objective; until then the Iter_19 review reports the chapters retrofitted as an observation of the existing objectives with the method text stating what was counted. (b) Cross.B of the research gates still cannot run (ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB); the research criterion of the retrofit therefore says: Cross.B must not FAIL, CANNOT_RUN is reported and is not a pass. (c) The chapter check of this register does not cover Deck and Page of chapters 1 to 5 (fact 3). (d) The end of Iter_19 is the proposed end of seven days (G9); a rebaseline is an owner decision, and 72.5 h of estimated work in seven days depends on how many executor sessions run side by side (the plan: decks and research of different chapters in parallel, browser tests serially); the plan does not promise that all five chapters finish inside it, and a chapter that is not Done at the review is said to be not Done and is carried by the change route, not hidden. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage is revised once more (G125 route 2). Iter_19 gets its start (the planning ceremony), its end (seven days, G9), its sprint goal, the five stories of chapters 1 to 5 (Ready, scored) and 30 tasks; the stories of chapters 10 to 25, the remaining-chapters story and the Cross.B gap story move to the new unstarted Iter_20; the planned retrofit criterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit is restated (planned into Iter_19; the page test 9.37.0; the manifest) and ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch is added; the exclusion ex:Excl2_NoRebuild is lifted for the NEW files of chapters 1 to 5 only. RE-RANKING of the open items (WSJF: business value 20; time criticality 20, 16, 13, 10, 8 in the owner's order of chapters; risk reduction = the number of deck-standard elements and research gates measured failing; job size 14.5 h): the order is chapter 1, 2, 3, 4, 5; inside a chapter the order of the dependencies (deck, deck control, page, research set and page ABox, research control, page control); the Iter_20 stories stay Proposed and unscored, in the owner's order (chapters 10 to 25, the remaining chapters), the Cross.B gap after a decision on what a hybrid chain of this course is. Not in the plan: a rebaseline, a waiver, an edit of a gate or test, a new metric." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog9 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: Iteration 19 planned for the retrofit of chapters 1 to 5, the later chapters moved to Iteration 20"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_Iter19, ex:IA2_Iter19 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed: close the Iteration 18 review, then plan and start the Iteration 19 retrofit from chapter 1 by the change route: re-rank the open items, generate the briefs, give the executor briefs to start; do not wait for the owner. The owner's decision of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC) (ex:CR2_Priority3), recorded as relayed, is the release: after chapters 7, 8 and 9 are finished, return to ALL chapters starting with chapter 1 (retrofit to the standard: deck, chapter-code manifest, page). Chapters 7, 8 and 9 and the repairs are finished and controlled (register 2.201.0). Stories become Ready with scores and tasks, a criterion is added and another restated, and stories move between iterations: the closed Backlog stage's digest moves (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request CR2_Iter19 and the impact assessment IA2_Iter19 were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR8 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR9 and re-admits every item without re-dating any; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR8 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "7edc09d" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR8 backlog:outputRetracted true .


ex:TK_Ret_Ch01_Deck_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the deck of chapter 1 (Python Basics) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ret_Ch01_Deck_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the deck of chapter 1 (Python Basics) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_19 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T01:43:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T02:01:46"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck01, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck01_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck01_1 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_DeckCheck ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: build the deck of chapter 1 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research (03-materials/ch01/rdodi, the newest research) and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard; the new deck goes to 03-materials/ch01/ named as the chapter's earlier decks are named; the earlier chapter 1 deck lives in 08-tooling/ch01-deck/ and stays where it is. The owner's teaching-material rules: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs (no text box over 30 words); explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes (at most 60 words); one smooth colour scheme; dividers that name their concepts with a line of meaning and a visual; coverage of the research concepts not below 90 percent. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch01/page/chapter_code_ch01_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code exactly as on the slide, the slide number, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file in 08-tooling/ch01-deck; the checker is the independent TK_Std_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I19-deck-ch01; estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch01_Deck_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 1 (Python Basics) as it stands: research 03-materials/ch01/rdodi (document v1_2_0, domain TBox v1_1_1, ABox v1_1_1, SHACL v1_0_1, research v1_1_0; there is NO data module for chapter 1 in 08-tooling, only the corpus sen0414_ch01_corpus_v1_2_0.py: write the data module like chapter 7 v1_3_0 from the corpus); newest deck 03-materials/ch01/SEN0414_Ch01_PythonBasics_3e_v3_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v3_0_0.py in 08-tooling/ch01-deck/); newest page 03-materials/ch01/page/sen0414_ch01_page_v9_28_0.html with page ABox v9_4_2; stories 08-tooling/sen0414_ch01_stories_v1_0_0.py; the first-program example of the old deck is 08-tooling/ch01-deck/first_program_v1_0_1.py. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25, from the repository; logs 08-tooling/control-iter19-logs/): (1) DECKS: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest deck of each chapter 1 to 5 prints FAILING: chapter 1 fails D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (8 of 13; M1 not measured, no manifest); chapter 2 the same 8; chapter 3 the same 8; chapter 4 the same 8; chapter 5 fails those 8 and D12 (9). Every chapter 1 to 5 has NO chapter-code manifest (03-materials/chNN/page has none) and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 ends FINDINGS on every one (5, 4, 6, 5 and 3 findings for chapters 1 to 5). (2) RESEARCH: the chapter check Research/Ch01 to Research/Ch05 each ends 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage1 to Stage3 PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (hollow typed individuals of the page ABox: 10, 10, 10, 11, 11) and Stage4.sub FAIL (individuals not substantive: 80, 81, 85, 78, 91), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN. It is the defect that chapter 6 had (ex:CR2_ResFix06); for chapters 1 to 5 the research is therefore part of the retrofit, not an extra. (3) THE CHAPTER CHECK does not cover chapters 1 to 5 for Deck and Page: Deck/Ch01 and Deck/Ch02 end in an assertion, Deck/Ch03 and Deck/Ch04 in a missing build script, Deck/Ch05 in StopIteration; Page/Ch01 starts a browser test outside the lock and was stopped. They are the chapters it was never written for (it covers 6 to 12 and chapter 6 partly). The controller measures chapters 1 to 5 with the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the page test 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0, and the chapter check Research/ChNN; adding Deck and Page cases to the chapter check is not part of this plan (a change to a committed tool; a new tool version would be a new item). (4) PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 1 to 5 are v9_28_0 (template 9.50.0, old standard); they have no chapter-code tab. The rebuilt pages follow the pages of chapters 6 to 9 (v9_90_0, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0, page test 9.37.0, runner v1_1_0). (5) PRECEDENT: chapter 9 (deck 2026-10-24 19:37 to 19:58; page 20:05 to 23:54) and chapter 6 (page, then the research repair, which took three executor sessions because the second dropped seven individuals of the old set without saying so: the controller compares the individual sets of the old and new files, and an executor must too). The first story photograph of the chapter 9 page fills the viewport height, so the story text starts below the fold: the retrofit pages must show the story text without scrolling past a full-height photograph (noted at the Iter_18 review). (6) ESTIMATES (G120: estimates, not measurements): deck build 5.0 h, deck verify 0.5 h, page build 3.5 h, research set and page ABox 4.0 h, research verify 0.5 h, page verify 1.0 h: 14.5 h per chapter, 72.5 h for the five; the machine has 2 cores and browser tests run one at a time, so the executor sessions of different chapters overlap only in the deck and research builds." .

