apters 1 to 5 with the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the page test 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0, and the chapter check Research/ChNN; adding Deck and Page cases to the chapter check is not part of this plan (a change to a committed tool; a new tool version would be a new item). (4) PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 1 to 5 are v9_28_0 (template 9.50.0, old standard); they have no chapter-code tab. The rebuilt pages follow the pages of chapters 6 to 9 (v9_90_0, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0, page test 9.37.0, runner v1_1_0). (5) PRECEDENT: chapter 9 (deck 2026-10-24 19:37 to 19:58; page 20:05 to 23:54) and chapter 6 (page, then the research repair, which took three executor sessions because the second dropped seven individuals of the old set without saying so: the controller compares the individual sets of the old and new files, and an executor must too). The first story photograph of the chapter 9 page fills the viewport height, so the story text starts below the fold: the retrofit pages must show the story text without scrolling past a full-height photograph (noted at the Iter_18 review). (6) ESTIMATES (G120: estimates, not measurements): deck build 5.0 h, deck verify 0.5 h, page build 3.5 h, research set and page ABox 4.0 h, research verify 0.5 h, page verify 1.0 h: 14.5 h per chapter, 72.5 h for the five; the machine has 2 cores and browser tests run one at a time, so the executor sessions of different chapters overlap only in the deck and research builds." .

