    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_19 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T01:43:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T02:01:46"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck03, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck03_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck03_1 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_DeckCheck ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: build the deck of chapter 3 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research (03-materials/ch03/rdodi, the newest research) and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard; the new deck goes to 03-materials/ch03/ named as the chapter's earlier decks are named; the earlier chapter 3 deck lives in 08-tooling/ch03-deck/ and stays where it is. The owner's teaching-material rules: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs (no text box over 30 words); explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes (at most 60 words); one smooth colour scheme; dividers that name their concepts with a line of meaning and a visual; coverage of the research concepts not below 90 percent. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch03/page/chapter_code_ch03_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code exactly as on the slide, the slide number, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file in 08-tooling/ch03-deck; the checker is the independent TK_Std_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I19-deck-ch03; estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control." .
