    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Ret_Ch03_Deck_Verify, ex:TK_Std_TemplateFix_Verify, ex:TK_Std_Runner_Verify, ex:TK_Std_Regress, ex:TK_Std_Charset_Verify, ex:TK_Std_PageTest37_Verify ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: Build the page of chapter 3 as a NEW file with a new page version (above 9_28_0; the pages of chapters 6 to 9 are v9_90_0) on the template 9.52.2 (08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_2.html) with the page builder v4_18_1 (08-tooling/sen0414_page_build_v4_18_1.py) and the page-data builder v2_25_0 (state how you passed the template), from the chapter research, the deck's lecture export and stories, and the deck's chapter-code manifest. Run the page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 (the runner sen0414_page_test_run_v1_1_0.py; PAGE_TEST_FILE=sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py for 9.37.0), serially, store the result as a new test_results file in 08-tooling/ch03-page, and run the chapter check Page/Ch09. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.37.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I19-page-ch03; estimated 3.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the deck of the chapter is controlled." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch03_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 3 (Loops) as it stands: research 03-materials/ch03/rdodi (document v1_2_0, domain TBox and ABox v1_1_0, SHACL v1_0_0, research v1_2_0; data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch03_rdodi_data_v1_0_0.py, corpus v1_0_0); newest deck 03-materials/ch03/SEN0414_Ch03_Loops_3e_v4_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v4_0_0.py in 08-tooling/ch03-deck/); newest page 03-materials/ch03/page/sen0414_ch03_page_v9_28_0.html with page ABox v1_5_0; stories 08-tooling/sen0414_ch03_stories_v1_0_0.py. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25, from the repository; logs 08-tooling/control-iter19-logs/): (1) DECKS: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest deck of each chapter 1 to 5 prints FAILING: chapter 1 fails D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (8 of 13; M1 not measured, no manifest); chapter 2 the same 8; chapter 3 the same 8; chapter 4 the same 8; chapter 5 fails those 8 and D12 (9). Every chapter 1 to 5 has NO chapter-code manifest (03-materials/chNN/page has none) and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 ends FINDINGS on every one (5, 4, 6, 5 and 3 findings for chapters 1 to 5). (2) RESEARCH: the chapter check Research/Ch01 to Research/Ch05 each ends 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage1 to Stage3 PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (hollow typed individuals of the page ABox: 10, 10, 10, 11, 11) and Stage4.sub FAIL (individuals not substantive: 80, 81, 85, 78, 91), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN. It is the defect that chapter 6 had (ex:CR2_ResFix06); for chapters 1 to 5 the research is therefore part of the retrofit, not an extra. (3) THE CHAPTER CHECK does not cover chapters 1 to 5 for Deck and Page: Deck/Ch01 and Deck/Ch02 end in an assertion, Deck/Ch03 and Deck/Ch04 in a missing build script, Deck/Ch05 in StopIteration; Page/Ch01 starts a browser test outside the lock and was stopped. They are the chapters it was never written for (it covers 6 to 12 and chapter 6 partly). The controller measures chapters 1 to 5 with the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the page test 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0, and the chapter check Research/ChNN; adding Deck and Page cases to the chapter check is not part of this plan (a change to a committed tool; a new tool version would be a new item). (4) PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 1 to 5 are v9_28_0 (template 9.50.0, old standard); they have no chapter-code tab. The rebuilt pages follow the pages of chapters 6 to 9 (v9_90_0, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0, page test 9.37.0, runner v1_1_0). (5) PRECEDENT: chapter 9 (deck 2026-10-24 19:37 to 19:58; page 20:05 to 23:54) and chapter 6 (page, then the research repair, which took three executor sessions because the second dropped seven individuals of the old set without saying so: the controller compares the individual sets of the old and new files, and an executor must too). The first story photograph of the chapter 9 page fills the viewport height, so the story text starts below the fold: the retrofit pages must show the story text without scrolling past a full-height photograph (noted at the Iter_18 review). (6) ESTIMATES (G120: estimates, not measurements): deck build 5.0 h, deck verify 0.5 h, page build 3.5 h, research set and page ABox 4.0 h, research verify 0.5 h, page verify 1.0 h: 14.5 h per chapter, 72.5 h for the five; the machine has 2 cores and browser tests run one at a time, so the executor sessions of different chapters overlap only in the deck and research builds." .

