    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: build the deck of chapter 4 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research (03-materials/ch04/rdodi, the newest research) and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard; the new deck goes to 03-materials/ch04/ named as the chapter's earlier decks are named; the earlier chapter 4 deck lives in 08-tooling/ch04-deck/ and stays where it is. The owner's teaching-material rules: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs (no text box over 30 words); explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes (at most 60 words); one smooth colour scheme; dividers that name their concepts with a line of meaning and a visual; coverage of the research concepts not below 90 percent. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch04/page/chapter_code_ch04_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code exactly as on the slide, the slide number, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file in 08-tooling/ch04-deck; the checker is the independent TK_Std_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I19-deck-ch04; estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch04_Deck_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 4 (Functions) as it stands: research 03-materials/ch04/rdodi (document v1_2_0, domain TBox and ABox v1_1_0, SHACL v1_0_0, research v1_1_0; data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch04_rdodi_data_v1_0_0.py, corpus v1_0_0); newest deck 03-materials/ch04/SEN0414_Ch04_Functions_3e_v2_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v2_0_0.py in 08-tooling/ch04-deck/); newest page 03-materials/ch04/page/sen0414_ch04_page_v9_28_0.html with page ABox v1_5_0; stories 08-tooling/sen0414_ch04_stories_v1_0_0.py. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25, from the repository; logs 08-tooling/control-iter19-logs/): (1) DECKS: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest deck of each chapter 1 to 5 prints FAILING: chapter 1 fails D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (8 of 13; M1 not measured, no manifest); chapter 2 the same 8; chapter 3 the same 8; chapter 4 the same 8; chapter 5 fails those 8 and D12 (9). Every chapter 1 to 5 has NO chapter-code manifest (03-materials/chNN/page has none) and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 ends FINDINGS on every one (5, 4, 6, 5 and 3 findings for chapters 1 to 5). (2) RESEARCH: the chapter check Research/Ch01 to Research/Ch05 each ends 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage1 to Stage3 PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (hollow typed individuals of the page ABox: 10, 10, 10, 11, 11) and Stage4.sub FAIL (individuals not substantive: 80, 81, 85, 78, 91), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN. It is the defect that chapter 6 had (ex:CR2_ResFix06); for chapters 1 to 5 the research is therefore part of the retrofit, not an extra. (3) THE CHAPTER CHECK does not cover chapters 1 to 5 for Deck and Page: Deck/Ch01 and Deck/Ch02 end in an assertion, Deck/Ch03 and Deck/Ch04 in a missing build script, Deck/Ch05 in StopIteration; Page/Ch01 starts a browser test outside the lock and was stopped. They are the chapters it was never written for (it covers 6 to 12 and chapter 6 partly). The controller measures chapters 1 to 5 with the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the page test 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0, and the chapter check Research/ChNN; adding Deck and Page cases to the chapter check is not part of this plan (a change to a committed tool; a new tool version would be a new item). (4) PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 1 to 5 are v9_28_0 (template 9.50.0, old standard); they have no chapter-code tab. The rebuilt pages follow the pages of chapters 6 to 9 (v9_90_0, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0, page test 9.37.0, runner v1_1_0). (5) PRECEDENT: chapter 9 (deck 2026-10-24 19:37 to 19:58; page 20:05 to 23:54) and chapter 6 (page, then the research repair, which took three executor sessions because the second dropped seven individuals of the old set without saying so: the controller compares the individual sets of the old and new files, and an executor must too). The first story photograph of the chapter 9 page fills the viewport height, so the story text starts below the fold: the retrofit pages must show the story text without scrolling past a full-height photograph (noted at the Iter_18 review). (6) ESTIMATES (G120: estimates, not measurements): deck build 5.0 h, deck verify 0.5 h, page build 3.5 h, research set and page ABox 4.0 h, research verify 0.5 h, page verify 1.0 h: 14.5 h per chapter, 72.5 h for the five; the machine has 2 cores and browser tests run one at a time, so the executor sessions of different chapters overlap only in the deck and research builds." .

