    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the research set of chapter 5 (Debugging) pass the chapter check Research/Ch05 on a NEW data version and a NEW page ABox that describes the NEW page. Read the criterion (ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch) and the precedent of chapter 6 first (commits 0064873, 12b4bd1, f18e3da, 86d4946, c1d3615; the data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_2_0.py; the page-ABox builder 08-tooling/sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_9.py; the chapter 7 data module v1_3_0 for the way a data module is made from a corpus). The lesson of chapter 6: a second session dropped seven individuals of the old set and said nothing was removed; before you report, compare the sets of individuals, classes, links, sources and labels of the OLD and the NEW files with a script and list every difference with its reason. Nothing is invented: content comes from the book's chapter, the deck, the page and the existing files. A committed file is never edited. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is reported as such and is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: no build beside a browser test. Planned session SEN0414-I19-research-ch05; estimated 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the page of the chapter is controlled (the page ABox describes the new page); the research set itself may be prepared earlier but its page ABox is built last." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch05_Research backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 5 (Debugging) as it stands: research 03-materials/ch05/rdodi (document v1_2_0, domain TBox and ABox v1_1_0, SHACL v1_0_0, research v1_1_0; data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch05_rdodi_data_v1_0_0.py, corpus v1_0_0); newest deck 03-materials/ch05/SEN0414_Ch05_Debugging_3e_v2_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v2_0_0.py in 08-tooling/ch05-deck/); newest page 03-materials/ch05/page/sen0414_ch05_page_v9_28_0.html with page ABox v1_3_0; stories 08-tooling/sen0414_ch05_stories_v1_0_0.py. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25, from the repository; logs 08-tooling/control-iter19-logs/): (1) DECKS: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest deck of each chapter 1 to 5 prints FAILING: chapter 1 fails D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (8 of 13; M1 not measured, no manifest); chapter 2 the same 8; chapter 3 the same 8; chapter 4 the same 8; chapter 5 fails those 8 and D12 (9). Every chapter 1 to 5 has NO chapter-code manifest (03-materials/chNN/page has none) and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 ends FINDINGS on every one (5, 4, 6, 5 and 3 findings for chapters 1 to 5). (2) RESEARCH: the chapter check Research/Ch01 to Research/Ch05 each ends 'OVERALL: FAIL (2)': Stage1 to Stage3 PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (hollow typed individuals of the page ABox: 10, 10, 10, 11, 11) and Stage4.sub FAIL (individuals not substantive: 80, 81, 85, 78, 91), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN. It is the defect that chapter 6 had (ex:CR2_ResFix06); for chapters 1 to 5 the research is therefore part of the retrofit, not an extra. (3) THE CHAPTER CHECK does not cover chapters 1 to 5 for Deck and Page: Deck/Ch01 and Deck/Ch02 end in an assertion, Deck/Ch03 and Deck/Ch04 in a missing build script, Deck/Ch05 in StopIteration; Page/Ch01 starts a browser test outside the lock and was stopped. They are the chapters it was never written for (it covers 6 to 12 and chapter 6 partly). The controller measures chapters 1 to 5 with the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the page test 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0, and the chapter check Research/ChNN; adding Deck and Page cases to the chapter check is not part of this plan (a change to a committed tool; a new tool version would be a new item). (4) PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 1 to 5 are v9_28_0 (template 9.50.0, old standard); they have no chapter-code tab. The rebuilt pages follow the pages of chapters 6 to 9 (v9_90_0, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0, page test 9.37.0, runner v1_1_0). (5) PRECEDENT: chapter 9 (deck 2026-10-24 19:37 to 19:58; page 20:05 to 23:54) and chapter 6 (page, then the research repair, which took three executor sessions because the second dropped seven individuals of the old set without saying so: the controller compares the individual sets of the old and new files, and an executor must too). The first story photograph of the chapter 9 page fills the viewport height, so the story text starts below the fold: the retrofit pages must show the story text without scrolling past a full-height photograph (noted at the Iter_18 review). (6) ESTIMATES (G120: estimates, not measurements): deck build 5.0 h, deck verify 0.5 h, page build 3.5 h, research set and page ABox 4.0 h, research verify 0.5 h, page verify 1.0 h: 14.5 h per chapter, 72.5 h for the five; the machine has 2 cores and browser tests run one at a time, so the executor sessions of different chapters overlap only in the deck and research builds." .

