ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck04 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 4 deck (new file SEN0414_Ch04_Functions_3e_v3_0_0.pptx, 46 slides, commit 30d1e77 of the executor session SEN0414-I19-deck-ch04): deck standard check 13 of 13 (the earlier deck failed 8), overlap check CLEAN (the earlier one had 5 findings), the chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch04_v1_0_0.json equals the deck's 25 code boxes in text and order, the 25 examples re-run now under Python 3.13.16 give the recorded results, the chapter folders gained 12 files and no committed file was modified since the planning commit 5136c8d, three story slides with their pictures (two photographs and the Python logo) and a provenance record; every one of the 46 slides viewed on the controller's own fresh render (numbered, analogy tables, three 5N1K stories each with a picture and a live link, native charts, a resources slide; no overflow seen; the code on slides 18 to 28 is small but whole and the chart axis labels of slide 39 are dense). The controller's first control script version (v1_0_0) wrongly required three photographs and failed this deck on that assertion alone; the assertion was corrected in a new file (v1_1_0, which counts photographs and logos against the story slides the deck check reports) and the control was re-run on all four decks with the same passes. Disclosed by the executor and recorded: the old recursion-limit, validate-at-the-door and annotations examples were not carried over (not research concepts; annotations and nonlocal are in the table of slide 43); no example shows a traceback or needs input(); the interpreter of the build is Python 3.13.16; rebuilding re-stamps the creation time of a file, and the executor restored the committed bytes with git checkout (the control compares the committed file)"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit ;
