ex:TK_Ret_Ch05_Deck_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Controlled by the lineage agent on 2026-10-25T02:07:53 UTC: the chapter 5 deck (new file SEN0414_Ch05_Debugging_3e_v3_0_0.pptx, 43 slides, commit 9d6f36e of the executor session SEN0414-I19-deck-ch05): deck standard check 13 of 13 (the earlier deck failed 9), overlap check CLEAN (the earlier one had 3 findings), the chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch05_v1_0_0.json equals the deck's 20 code boxes in text and order, the 20 examples re-run now under Python 3.13.16 give the recorded results, the chapter folders gained 11 files and no committed file was modified since the planning commit 5136c8d, three story slides with their pictures (the 1947 logbook page, a photograph and the Python logo) and a provenance record; every one of the 43 slides viewed on the controller's own fresh render (numbered, analogy tables, three 5N1K stories each with a picture and a live link, native charts, a resources slide; no overflow seen; the code on the boxprint and stepper slides 7, 14 and 37 is set at 9.5 pt, small but whole, and is recorded as a legibility observation for teaching, not a standard failure since D2 and D12 pass). Disclosed by the executor and recorded: the logging examples use force=True because the browser's Python keeps logging state; the stepper uses sys.settrace and the breakpoint example swaps sys.breakpointhook, and they were not run in the browser's Python, so the page test decides whether they run there (a known risk for the page task); the boxprint code is split into four boxes so that no box passes 30 words; the resources slide has no video link (the video site answered 429); the executor's git remote notice says the repository moved to https://github.com/altunelyusuf/AdvancedProgrammingWithPython.git. Evidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck05, verified by backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0." .
