ex:CR2_ErrFirst a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Page test 9.37.0 fails on an example whose recorded result begins with an error message (chapters 1, 3 and 4): new deck and manifest versions with the error shown after an ordinary result line"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed (executor SEN0414-I19-page-ch03 stopped with a failure of the page test 9.37.0, commits 2afb447 and 9801f99): find the root cause, decide by the rules without waiting for the owner among a new deck/manifest version, a new template version or a test finding; no gate edited or weakened, a failing result is not worked around; use the change route and re-rank; disclose that 9.37.0 failed on a new chapter. The owner's standing rules that repairs re-rank the open items and that every example's executed result is shown as a visualisation also hold. The scope does not move outward: the retrofit of chapters 1 to 5 is the scope; what is added is one repair story with three deck-fix tasks and a controller task." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_ErrFirst a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the error-first repair changes in the iteration, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_ErrFirst ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25): (1) the executor of the chapter 3 page reports 9.34.0 PASS (382 features, 0 failed) and 9.37.0 FAIL on the single feature P2 'every chapter-code example opens in the editor, runs in the page ... and shows a visualised result': '22 of 22 examples ran; 1 defects 17 A module that cannot be found: result is text, not a visualisation'; the executor of the chapter 1 page, still running, has the same single defect on example 14 'Errors that teach' (its log 08-tooling/ch01-page/logs_iter19/page_test_9_37_0_run1_full_output.log); the chapter 2 page passes the feature. (2) CAUSE, read from the files: the recorded expected result of chapter 3 example 17 in 03-materials/ch03/page/chapter_code_ch03_v1_0_0.json is 'ModuleNotFoundError - No module named nosuchmodule' on its FIRST line; the template 9.52.2 function ccVisual (in every v9_90_0 page) sets err = /^(\\w*Error|Traceback|Stopped after)/ on the trimmed output and draws no chart then, so the page shows the text (which equals the slide, correct); the page test 9.37.0 (lines 1604 to 1606 of sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py) tests the error name only with the pattern 'Traceback|NameError|Error:' (a colon), so the form 'ModuleNotFoundError -' is not seen as an error, and for 'ValueError: ...' (chapter 1 example 14) the name passes as expected but the next line still demands a visual; an expected error that is the FIRST line therefore always fails. Why chapters 6 to 9 passed: every example of theirs that shows an error prints it after an ordinary line (chapter 6 example 2 'e 3' then IndexError; chapter 1 examples 9, 10 and 11 print ordinary lines first and pass); the change request ex:CR2_Retest37 built 9.37.0 on the chapter 6 case. (3) A scan of all five retrofit manifests (03-materials/ch0[1-5]/page/chapter_code_ch0N_v1_0_0.json) for a recorded result whose first line matches the template's pattern finds exactly three: chapter 1 example 14, chapter 3 example 17, chapter 4 example 17 ('UnboundLocalError NameError'); chapters 2 and 5 have none. (4) The executor of the chapter 3 page added 08-tooling/ch03-deck/examples_out_v3_0_0.json (a new file, committed in 2afb447, input of the page-data builder): the controller checked it - 22 examples, ids equal to the manifest's in order, the code of every example equal to the manifest's, no committed file modified. (5) The three options: a TEST change (accept text for an expected error) would weaken a gate that was just controlled; a TEMPLATE change (draw a chart for an expected error) would make a new template version that the pages of chapters 1 to 5 and 6 to 9 are not built on; neither is chosen. The decks' content is the free variable: the owner's rule shows every executed result as a visualisation, and an error example is better taught with a visible line before the error message. DISCLOSURE: the page test 9.37.0 failed on a new chapter. It is a FINDING about the interplay of the test and the template (an expected error as the first line cannot satisfy the test); it is reported openly, the test and the template are not edited, and the finding is not worked around. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage is revised once more (G125 route 2): one story, one criterion, test cases and four tasks are added to Iteration 19; the page-verify tasks of chapters 1, 3 and 4 gain the dependency on the controller task; the deck-verify tasks already Done stay Done and are not re-dated (the controlled decks 4.0.0, 5.0.0 and 3.0.0 stay as history); the page-build tasks of chapters 1, 3 and 4 are in progress and are re-briefed: they are controlled only on the manifest 1.1.0 (chapter 3 and 1 after their executors rebuild); chapters 2 and 5 are not affected. RE-RANKING (WSJF, the owner's rule that repairs re-rank the open items): the repair story, which blocks the control of the pages of chapters 1, 3 and 4, ranks first; the five chapter stories are re-scored with the risk reduction of chapters 1, 3 and 4 raised by the measured defect. Not in the plan: a waiver, an edit of a gate, test or template, a rebaseline." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog10 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: the error-first repair of the decks of chapters 1, 3 and 4"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_ErrFirst, ex:IA2_ErrFirst ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed (executor SEN0414-I19-page-ch03 stopped with a failure of the page test 9.37.0, commits 2afb447 and 9801f99): find the root cause, decide by the rules without waiting for the owner among a new deck/manifest version, a new template version or a test finding; no gate edited or weakened, a failing result is not worked around; use the change route and re-rank; disclose that 9.37.0 failed on a new chapter. The owner's standing rules that repairs re-rank the open items and that every example's executed result is shown as a visualisation also hold. A story, a criterion, test cases and four tasks are added to the closed Backlog stage and the dependencies and scores of open items move: its digest moves (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request and the impact assessment were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out2_BacklogR9 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as ex:Out2_BacklogR10 and re-admits every item without re-dating any; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR9 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "439d2b4" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR9 backlog:outputRetracted true .

