ex:TC2E_Passes a backlog:TestCase ; rdfs:label "Run the deck checks and the example runs on the new decks of chapters 1, 3 and 4; the controller re-runs them"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:exercisesCriterion ex:AC2R_ErrFirst ; backlog:coversScenario ex:Scen2S_D_Passes ; backlog:runsOnData ex:Data2E_Passing ;
    backlog:hasCaseText "The deck standard check prints 13 of 13 PASS including M1 and the overlap check CLEAN on each new deck; the manifests 1.1.0 differ from 1.0.0 in one example each; every example runs under Python 3.13 to its recorded result; no recorded first line of chapters 1 to 5 begins with an error name." .
ex:TC2E_NotClaimed a backlog:TestCase ; rdfs:label "Scan the committed manifests 1.0.0 and require the scan to find the three examples"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:exercisesCriterion ex:AC2R_ErrFirst ; backlog:coversScenario ex:Scen2S_D_NotClaimed ; backlog:runsOnData ex:Data2E_Failing ;
    backlog:hasCaseText "The scan over the committed manifests 1.0.0 of chapters 1 to 5 finds chapter 1 example 14, chapter 3 example 17 and chapter 4 example 17, and the page test 9.37.0 on the chapter 3 page fails the P2 run feature on example 17 (the executor's log and the controller's re-run): the scan is not a tool that passes everything." .
ex:Data2E_Passing a backlog:TestData ; rdfs:label "The new decks and manifests 1.1.0 of chapters 1, 3 and 4"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasFixtureState "The committed new decks and manifests; the controlled decks and manifests 1.0.0 as history." .
ex:Data2E_Failing a backlog:TestData ; rdfs:label "The committed manifests 1.0.0 of chapters 1 to 5 and the chapter 3 page v9_90_0"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasFixtureState "Committed files, unchanged." .

ex:AC2R_ErrFirst a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "No chapter-code example of chapters 1 to 5 has a recorded result that begins with an error message, so that the page shows every result as a visualisation and the page test 9.37.0 is not failed by it"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the decks 4.0.0 (chapter 1), 5.0.0 (chapter 3) and 3.0.0 (chapter 4), controlled as Done, whose chapter-code manifests 1.0.0 record, for chapter 1 example 14, chapter 3 example 17 and chapter 4 example 17, a result that BEGINS with an error name (the template draws text, not a visualisation, and the page test 9.37.0 fails the P2 run feature), when for each of the three chapters a NEW deck version (4.1.0, 5.1.0, 3.1.0) is built as a new file with a NEW manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_1_0.json in which only that example is changed - its code prints an ordinary result line first and the error message after it, the slide shows the same code and result and the explanation clue is kept - then ALL of: (1) every file is new and every committed file is byte-identical; (2) the deck standard check v1_0_0 prints 13 of 13 PASS including M1, and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 prints CLEAN, on each new deck; (3) the new manifest differs from 1.0.0 in that one example only (code and expected), every other example, name, order and concept link identical, and equals the deck's code boxes (M1); (4) every example of the manifest run now under Python 3.13 prints its recorded expected result, and in no manifest of chapters 1 to 5 does the first line of a recorded result match ^(\\w*Error|Traceback|Stopped after) (the controller scans all five); (5) the controller renders the changed slide and reads it; (6) the pages of chapters 1, 3 and 4 are built on the manifests 1.1.0 and the controller's page test 9.37.0 on them ends with no failed feature (that is the criterion of their page-build tasks); no gate, test or template is edited." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS2_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS2_DeckOverlap, ex:TS2_PageTest37 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0; deck overlap check v1_0_0; page test 9.37.0 through runner v1_1_0; Python 3.13 for the example runs" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the controller's own runs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC2E_Passes, ex:TC2E_NotClaimed .

ex:ST_Ret_ErrFirstFix a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Repair: the decks of chapters 1, 3 and 4 show the error message of an error example after an ordinary result line"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_Ret_ErrFirstFix" ;
    backlog:hasTitle "Repair: the decks of chapters 1, 3 and 4 show the error message of an error example after an ordinary result line" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_19 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Maintenance ;
    backlog:asRole "SEN0414 instructor" ; backlog:wantsCapability "an error example whose recorded result starts with an ordinary line, so the page can draw it" ; backlog:soThat "every example of the chapter shows its executed result as a visualisation on the page, as the deck does" ;
    backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del2_StdDecks ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj2_StdDecks ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC2R_ErrFirst ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_Ret_Ch01_Deck_Fix, ex:TK_Ret_Ch03_Deck_Fix, ex:TK_Ret_Ch04_Deck_Fix, ex:TK_Ret_ErrFirst_Verify ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T03:22:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T03:34:27"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-25T08:49:24"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score11_ST_Ret_ErrFirstFix ; backlog:standsAlone true ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed (executor SEN0414-I19-page-ch03 stopped with a failure of the page test 9.37.0, commits 2afb447 and 9801f99): find the root cause, decide by the rules without waiting for the owner among a new deck/manifest version, a new template version or a test finding; no gate edited or weakened, a failing result is not worked around; use the change route and re-rank; disclose that 9.37.0 failed on a new chapter. The owner's standing rules that repairs re-rank the open items and that every example's executed result is shown as a visualisation also hold. MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25): (1) the executor of the chapter 3 page reports 9.34.0 PASS (382 features, 0 failed) and 9.37.0 FAIL on the single feature P2 'every chapter-code example opens in the editor, runs in the page ... and shows a visualised result': '22 of 22 examples ran; 1 defects 17 A module that cannot be found: result is text, not a visualisation'; the executor of the chapter 1 page, still running, has the same single defect on example 14 'Errors that teach' (its log 08-tooling/ch01-page/logs_iter19/page_test_9_37_0_run1_full_output.log); the chapter 2 page passes the feature. (2) CAUSE, read from the files: the recorded expected result of chapter 3 example 17 in 03-materials/ch03/page/chapter_code_ch03_v1_0_0.json is 'ModuleNotFoundError - No module named nosuchmodule' on its FIRST line; the template 9.52.2 function ccVisual (in every v9_90_0 page) sets err = /^(\\w*Error|Traceback|Stopped after)/ on the trimmed output and draws no chart then, so the page shows the text (which equals the slide, correct); the page test 9.37.0 (lines 1604 to 1606 of sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py) tests the error name only with the pattern 'Traceback|NameError|Error:' (a colon), so the form 'ModuleNotFoundError -' is not seen as an error, and for 'ValueError: ...' (chapter 1 example 14) the name passes as expected but the next line still demands a visual; an expected error that is the FIRST line therefore always fails. Why chapters 6 to 9 passed: every example of theirs that shows an error prints it after an ordinary line (chapter 6 example 2 'e 3' then IndexError; chapter 1 examples 9, 10 and 11 print ordinary lines first and pass); the change request ex:CR2_Retest37 built 9.37.0 on the chapter 6 case. (3) A scan of all five retrofit manifests (03-materials/ch0[1-5]/page/chapter_code_ch0N_v1_0_0.json) for a recorded result whose first line matches the template's pattern finds exactly three: chapter 1 example 14, chapter 3 example 17, chapter 4 example 17 ('UnboundLocalError NameError'); chapters 2 and 5 have none. (4) The executor of the chapter 3 page added 08-tooling/ch03-deck/examples_out_v3_0_0.json (a new file, committed in 2afb447, input of the page-data builder): the controller checked it - 22 examples, ids equal to the manifest's in order, the code of every example equal to the manifest's, no committed file modified. (5) The three options: a TEST change (accept text for an expected error) would weaken a gate that was just controlled; a TEMPLATE change (draw a chart for an expected error) would make a new template version that the pages of chapters 1 to 5 and 6 to 9 are not built on; neither is chosen. The decks' content is the free variable: the owner's rule shows every executed result as a visualisation, and an error example is better taught with a visible line before the error message. DISCLOSURE: the page test 9.37.0 failed on a new chapter. It is a FINDING about the interplay of the test and the template (an expected error as the first line cannot satisfy the test); it is reported openly, the test and the template are not edited, and the finding is not worked around." .
