    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T03:22:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T03:34:27"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deckfix01, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deckfix01_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deckfix01_1 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Ret_Ch01_Deck_Verify ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT REPAIR: build a NEW version of the deck of chapter 01 (Python Basics), 4.1.0 over the controlled 4.0.0, and a NEW chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch01/page/chapter_code_ch01_v1_1_0.json, changing ONLY example 14 'Errors that teach'. The cause: the recorded result of that example begins with an error message; the page template draws no chart for an output that begins with an error, so the page test 9.37.0 fails its P2 run feature for it (the page shows the error text, which equals the slide). The change: edit the example's code so that it first prints an ordinary result line (a value, a type, a count - something the example's lesson uses) and prints the error message after it, so the recorded result's FIRST line is not an error name; the error message stays in the result and on the slide, and the explanation clue on the slide is updated to match. Do it by a NEW version of the deck generator and of the example data (new files over the ones of the controlled deck; read how the controlled deck 08-tooling/ch01-deck/ was built), not by editing a committed file. Change nothing else: every other slide, example, name, order, concept link, story and picture is that of the controlled deck. Prove, and report as printed: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the new deck (13 of 13 PASS including M1); the deck overlap check v1_0_0 (CLEAN); a script comparing manifest 1.0.0 and 1.1.0 that lists every difference (exactly the one example); every example of the new manifest run under /usr/bin/python3.13 prints its recorded result; a scan that no recorded first line of the manifest matches ^(\\\\w*Error|Traceback|Stopped after); the generator's self-check. Do not touch the page, the page data or any research file: the page-build executor of this chapter rebuilds the page on the new manifest after the lineage agent controls your deck. A committed file is never edited; STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing one, a gate, a test, a template or a threshold. Report commit SHAs and the verbatim output of every run, and say what failed if anything. Planned session SEN0414-I19-deckfix-ch01; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

