ex:Ev2_Ctl_research03 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 3 research set and page ABox (new files: document, domain TBox, ABox, SHACL and research v1_3_0 in 03-materials/ch03/rdodi and the page ABox sen0414_ch03_page_abox_v9_91_0.ttl, commits ddf8ddd, 69323ba and 9ce7143 of the executor session SEN0414-I19-research-ch03, with the new data module, restore script, subset proof, page-ABox builder v1_1_12 and the compare tool): the controller's own chapter check Research/Ch03 ends PASS (the gates OVERALL PASS with Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS on the new page ABox, HermiT consistent, 0 mismatches; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN with 0 hybrid chains, reported and NOT counted as a pass), Research/Ch02 and Research/Ch05 to Research/Ch09 and the other retrofitted chapter still PASS on the controller's own runs, the page file is byte-identical to its controlled commit, and no committed file was modified since the planning commit 5136c8d; the controller's own comparison by local name: research files old against new - no individual, class, source or label missing and the 9 missing links are version metadata only; 235 and 235 individuals, 74 and 74 classes, 311 and 329 labels in the research files; page ABox old (v1_5_0, 113 individuals) against new (v9_91_0, 238) with the prefix s_ mapped - no individual and no predicate missing, exactly the 36 stated widget source links (to the whole document, now to the concept's own section) and the 19 stated reworded labels are missing. THE COORDINATOR'S QUESTION (95 execution checks against 200 for chapter 4): the controller read the data module and ran the chapter's corpus programs itself - the old data module 1_0_0 had a smaller taxonomy and its executed claims are kept (1_3_0 states that it adds to them, none removed); the corpus holds 200 checks of which the data module carries those that need no helper function, and the others run in the corpus's own program, which the controller ran to the end under Python 3.14.6: 233 claims executed, failures [] (log corpus_main_ch03.log) - so no claim is left unchecked, but 105 of the corpus's 200 checks are not run by the gate's execution checks; that is a limit of the generic check and is said here, not a failure. Disclosed by the executor and recorded: the builder v1_1_11 failed on the visual kind 'names' and was fixed in the new file v1_1_12; an earlier page-test run of the executor was cut off by its own time limit (log kept)."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch ;
