ex:Ev2_Ctl_research04 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 4 research set and page ABox (new files: document, domain TBox, ABox, SHACL and research v1_3_0 in 03-materials/ch04/rdodi and the page ABox sen0414_ch04_page_abox_v9_91_0.ttl, commits b98b045, 4e28f7e and 532c455 of the executor session SEN0414-I19-research-ch04, with the new data module, restore script, subset proof and compare tool; the page-ABox builder v1_1_11 unchanged): the controller's own chapter check Research/Ch04 ends PASS (the gates OVERALL PASS with Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS on the new page ABox, HermiT consistent, 0 mismatches; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN with 0 hybrid chains, reported and NOT counted as a pass), Research/Ch02 and Research/Ch05 to Research/Ch09 and the other retrofitted chapter still PASS on the controller's own runs, the page file is byte-identical to its controlled commit, and no committed file was modified since the planning commit 5136c8d; the controller's own comparison by local name: research files old against new - no individual, class, source or label missing and the 9 missing links are version metadata only; 254 and 254 individuals, 76 and 76 classes, 332 and 355 labels in the research files; page ABox old (v1_5_0, 118 individuals) against new (v9_91_0, 244) with the prefix s_ mapped - no individual and no predicate missing; the 27 missing links are the 24 stated widget source links (to the whole document, now to the concept's own section) and 3 links of the widget w_CallStackOrder (enforcesDomainConstraint, numericModelStatus Validated, instantiatesPrimitive CoupledVariableExplorer); the 18 missing labels are the 18 stated reworded ones. THE COORDINATOR'S QUESTION (are the 3 gone links acceptable): the old widget was a predict demonstrator over a stand-in expression, len(str(42 / 2)), that the old data module gave the concept - it did not demonstrate the order of calls; the corpus gives CallStackOrder no input and output example, so the new page shows a static example (honest) and the call-stack behaviour is still executed by the execution checks (call order, call stack depth). The controller judges the stated reason sufficient for the criterion (every difference has a reason), and says openly that the page has no live call-stack demonstrator now: a real one is an enhancement of the page for a later version, not a repair, and is NOT a requirement of the criterion. The chapter's corpus programs run to the end without a failure on the controller's own run (178 claims, log corpus_main_ch04.log). DISCLOSURE OF A FLAKY CHECK: the controller's FIRST run of Research/Ch04 (log rc3_Research_Ch04_run1_FAIL_under_load.log) ended FAIL with a mismatch on a claim that sends SIGINT to a child process and requires the answer within 3 seconds, while page tests and a corpus run were loading the two cores; three re-runs at a load of about 1.7 (the last one is the log rc3_Research_Ch04.log) end PASS with 200 checks and 0 mismatches. The claim is timing-sensitive (a 0.3 s wait, a 3 s limit); it is a latent flaw of the corpus check, not edited here; a research check that passes only when the machine is not busy is reported as that. The mismatch is recorded, not worked around: the PASS is on an unloaded re-run."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch ;
