nd PackageManager lost the link to the guided walkthrough primitive because page 9.92.0 shows these examples as static examples next to the real code tab; the controller judges the stated reason sufficient for the criterion (every difference has a reason) - the chapter-code tab runs the 19 examples of the manifest for real and the execution checks run them - and says openly that these six concepts have no step-through walkthrough on the page now: a walkthrough is an enhancement of the page for a later version, not a repair, and is NOT a requirement of the criterion. THE QUESTION OF UNCHECKED CLAIMS: the gate runs 66 checks; the chapter's corpus program holds 51 claims, which the controller ran to the end under Python 3.14.6: 51 claims executed, failures [] (log corpus_main_ch01.log) - no claim is left unchecked. Disclosed by the executor and recorded: the builder v1_1_13 is a new file because v1_1_11 and v1_1_12 stopped on the visual kind floatbits."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch ;
