ex:TK_Ret_Ch01_Research backlog:hasAuditNote "Controlled by the lineage agent on 2026-10-25T08:26:21 UTC: the chapter 1 research set and page ABox (new files: document, domain TBox, ABox, SHACL and research v1_3_0 in 03-materials/ch01/rdodi and the page ABox sen0414_ch01_page_abox_v9_92_0.ttl, commits 5e442f9, 0583fd9 and d681edb of the executor session SEN0414-I19-research-ch01, with the data module v1_3_0, restore v1_3_0 (keeps the old research namespace names), subset proof, compare tool and the NEW page-ABox builder v1_1_13 - v1_1_11 and v1_1_12 stopped on the visual kind floatbits): the controller's own chapter check Research/Ch01 ends PASS (OVERALL PASS with Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS on the new page ABox, HermiT consistent, 0 mismatches; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN with 0 hybrid chains, reported and NOT counted as a pass), Research/Ch02 to Research/Ch09 still PASS on the controller's own runs, the page file is byte-identical to its controlled commit c961ae7, no committed file was modified since the planning commit 5136c8d and everything of the chapter is committed; the controller's own comparison by local name: research files old against new - 168 and 168 individuals, 51 and 51 classes, 221 and 228 labels, nothing missing; the 10 missing links are version metadata only and the one missing source is the ontology-header reference to the RDODI procedure (as in chapter 2); the predicate comment is missing because the old header carried version notes of its own as comments (header metadata, observation); page ABox old (v9_4_2, 100 individuals) against new (v9_92_0, 171) with the prefix s_ mapped - no individual and no predicate missing, exactly the 35 stated widget source links (to the whole document, now to the concept's own section), the 6 stated links of step-through primitives and the 13 stated reworded labels are missing. THE COORDINATOR'S QUESTION (the 6 lost primitives, as the 3 links of chapter 4): the widgets Assignment, FreeThreadedBuild, Input, InteractiveShell, Output and PackageManager lost the link to the guided walkthrough primitive because page 9.92.0 shows these examples as static examples next to the real code tab; the controller judges the stated reason sufficient for the criterion (every difference has a reason) - the chapter-code tab runs the 19 examples of the manifest for real and the execution checks run them - and says openly that these six concepts have no step-through walkthrough on the page now: a walkthrough is an enhancement of the page for a later version, not a repair, and is NOT a requirement of the criterion. THE QUESTION OF UNCHECKED CLAIMS: the gate runs 66 checks; the chapter's corpus program holds 51 claims, which the controller ran to the end under Python 3.14.6: 51 claims executed, failures [] (log corpus_main_ch01.log) - no claim is left unchecked. Disclosed by the executor and recorded: the builder v1_1_13 is a new file because v1_1_11 and v1_1_12 stopped on the visual kind floatbits.. Evidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_research01, verified by backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0." .
