ex:RC2_Iter_19 a backlog:SprintReviewCeremony ; rdfs:label "Review of iteration 19: the chapter 1 to 5 retrofit closed"@en ; backlog:ceremonyFor ex:Iter_19 ; backlog:reviewsCeremony ex:PC2_Iter_19 ; backlog:closesIteration ex:Iter_19 ;
    backlog:closesStory ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch01, ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch02, ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch03, ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch04, ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch05, ex:ST_Ret_ErrFirstFix ; backlog:heldAt "2026-10-25T08:49:24"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "Held 2026-10-25T08:49:24 UTC by the lineage agent, on the controlled work of the iteration: ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch01, ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch02, ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch03, ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch04, ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch05, ST_Ret_ErrFirstFix are closed, each with all its tasks Done on bridge-verified evidence (register 2.218.0 to 2.232.0). Every member of the iteration is Done, so the iteration is closed. READINGS MEASURED IN THIS RUN (the metric observations read chapters 6, 7 and 8 as the metrics are defined; these are the chapters 1 to 5): decks of chapters 1 to 5 that pass the deck standard check 13 of 13 and the overlap check CLEAN: 5 of 5 (chapter 01: SEN0414_Ch01_PythonBasics_3e_v4_1_0.pptx: SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings); chapter 02: SEN0414_Ch02_FlowControl_3e_v4_0_0.pptx: SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings); chapter 03: SEN0414_Ch03_Loops_3e_v5_1_0.pptx: SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings); chapter 04: SEN0414_Ch04_Functions_3e_v3_1_0.pptx: SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings); chapter 05: SEN0414_Ch05_Debugging_3e_v3_0_0.pptx: SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0; overlap RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)); pages of chapters 1 to 5 whose control check (page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 on the controller's own serial runs, chapter-code tab equals the manifest, story layout rule) passes: 5 of 5; research sets of chapters 1 to 5 whose control check (chapter check Research/ChNN, old/new comparison by local name, corpus programs) passes: 5 of 5. NOT DONE, said openly: (1) Cross.B of the chapter checks is CANNOT_RUN in every chapter (0 hybrid chains) and is not counted as a pass - it is carried by ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB in Iteration 20; (2) the metrics of Obj2 still name chapters 6, 7 and 8 - widening them is the Owner's decision and no Rebaseline is written; (3) the page of chapter 4 has no live call-stack demonstrator (3 links of one widget gone) and the page of chapter 1 has no step-through walkthrough for 6 concepts: the stated reasons were accepted as sufficient for the criterion, the walkthroughs are enhancements, not repairs; (4) the chapter 3 EWD831 archive link is unreachable from this machine (open disclosure); (5) the corpus check of chapter 4 that sends SIGINT to a child process (0.3 s wait, 3 s limit) fails when the machine is loaded - a latent defect of the check, passes on three unloaded re-runs, not worked around; (6) the gate's generic execution check does not run every corpus check of chapters 3 and 4 (the corpus programs were run by the controller instead, failures none); (7) chapters 6 to 9 are covered by the earlier iteration and chapters 10 to 25 and the remaining chapters are not started: they are Iteration 20. Nothing of Iteration 19 is carried over."@en .
ex:Finding2_Iter19_MetricScope a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The retrofit of chapters 1 to 5 could not move the metrics it is tied to, which count chapters 6, 7 and 8 only"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch01 ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch02 ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch03 ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch04 ; backlog:relatesToWorkItem ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch05 ; backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_Methodology ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The bracketing observations of Met2_StdDecks and Met2_StdPages read 3 before and 3 after the retrofit stories, and the stories read as an ineffective corrective action. They are not: the objectives Obj2_StdDecks and Obj2_StdPages name decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8, and the stories of Iteration 19 bring chapters 1 to 5 to the same standard, so they cannot change a count of chapters 6 to 8. The stories are tied to these objectives because no objective names chapters 1 to 5 (the planning of Iteration 19 used the nearest objective). The work itself is measured and passes: 5 of 5 decks, 5 of 5 pages and 5 of 5 research sets at the review." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not a repair of the work. The metrics and their targets are the Owner's: widening them to chapters 1 to 25 is an open owner decision, and no Rebaseline is written here. Until it is taken, the readings of chapters 1 to 5 are in the method text of the observations and in the ceremony's comment, and Iteration 20 carries the same limit: its stories for chapters 10 to 25 will be tied to the same objectives and read the same way." .

ex:CR2_Iter20 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Plan Iteration 20: the retrofit of chapters 10 to 25 to the written standard, the Cross.B gap as a pilot, and the withdrawal of the story of the remaining chapters"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope2 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed: the Iteration 19 close is accepted; run the Iteration 20 change route now without waiting for the owner: check the stories against the verified gaps, change request and impact assessment, re-rank in the owner's order, generate the briefs from the current generator with the lessons of Iteration 19 folded in (new tool files from the start, the page-ABox builder v1_1_13, the page-ABox version above the old one, the story-layout probe on every story, the first-line error scan on manifests, the executor's own probe as strict as the controller's); plan the batches so that at most three executors run at once (two cores; the serial page-test lock was the bottleneck of Iteration 19; decks and research in parallel, page tests the only serial part). The owner's decision of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC) (ex:CR2_Priority3), recorded as relayed, is the release: after chapters 7, 8 and 9, return to ALL chapters (chapters 1 to 5 are done and controlled), and after that build all remaining chapters. The scope does not move outward: the planned stories were admitted at the owner's decision (ex:CR2_Priority3); this change plans them, adds the tasks, one criterion for the research set of chapters 10 to 25, and withdraws the story that has nothing left to build." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA2_Iter20 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What planning Iteration 20 changes, with the facts measured before it is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR2_Iter20 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (the lineage agent, 2026-10-25, from the repository and from its own runs; logs 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/): (1) THE STORY OF THE REMAINING CHAPTERS (ex:ST_Plan_Remaining) waited for a measurement 'when the retrofits finish': the repository holds, for each of the 25 chapters of the course (the 3rd edition's 24 chapters and the threads chapter 25 of the 2nd edition), research files, a deck and a page; no chapter lacks one of the three. The story has nothing to build and is withdrawn (Cancelled with its rationale); a chapter found lacking later is a new story by the change route. (2) DECKS of chapters 10 to 25 are NOT in 03-materials: each has one earlier deck 08-tooling/chNN-deck/sen0414_chNN_deck_v1_0_x.pptx (and its generator there); the deck standard check v1_0_0 prints 7 or 8 failing elements on every one (D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D11, and D12 for chapters 12 and 13; D10 and M1 not measured: no manifest), and the overlap check ends FINDINGS only for chapter 10 (2 findings). None has a chapter-code manifest. (3) PAGES: the newest pages are v9_28_0 to v9_35_0 (template 9.50.0 and older), with no chapter-code tab; no chapter 10 to 25 has a page ABox, so the gates' Stage 4 (A, B, cov, sub, src) and Cross.B have never run for them. (4) RESEARCH: the chapter check Research/Ch10 to Ch25 on the controller's machine ends PASS for chapters 10, 11, 12, 13 and 16 (the gates' Stages 1 to 3 and the execution checks pass) and FAIL for chapters 14, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24 and 25: the gates end OVERALL: PASS but the execution checks of the data module end with exit 1 (mismatches or a crash of the claim runner; chapter 14: openpyxl alone, Pillow absent, defusedxml absent; the claims were recorded on another environment). Per chapter: chapter 10: deck 7 failing elements, overlap FINDINGS, research PASS (0 mismatches); chapter 11: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research PASS (0 mismatches); chapter 12: deck 8 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research PASS (0 mismatches); chapter 13: deck 8 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research PASS (0 mismatches); chapter 14: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (2 mismatches); chapter 15: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (2 mismatches); chapter 16: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research PASS (0 mismatches); chapter 17: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (4 mismatches); chapter 18: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (1 mismatches); chapter 19: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (0 mismatches); chapter 20: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (3 mismatches); chapter 21: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (4 mismatches); chapter 22: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (5 mismatches); chapter 23: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (1 mismatches); chapter 24: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (0 mismatches); chapter 25: deck 7 failing elements, overlap CLEAN, research FAIL (0 mismatches). (5) THE CHAPTER CHECK has Deck and Page cases for some of these chapters; they were not run for chapters 10 to 25 here and are not part of the controller's measure (the controller measures with the deck standard check, the overlap check, the page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the runner v1_1_0 and the chapter check Research/ChNN). (6) FROM ITERATION 19 (the lessons, measured in its work): a committed control or build tool was edited in place twice; a first page failed the page test on an example whose recorded result began with an error line (six pages and decks repaired); a first page put the story text below the fold at 1366x768 (two pages); a page-ABox builder stopped on a visual kind it did not know three times (names, floatbits); a research check passed only on an unloaded machine (a signal-timing claim); each is written into the task notes below. GAPS SAID OPENLY: (a) the metrics Met2_StdDecks and Met2_StdPages count the decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 (target 3) and read 3 and 3; the retrofit of chapters 10 to 25 moves no number of them, as that of chapters 1 to 5 did not (ex:Finding2_Iter19_MetricScope); widening them is the Owner's decision and no rebaseline is written; the review of Iteration 20 reports the chapters as readings in the method text. (b) Cross.B of the research gates cannot run in any chapter (0 hybrid chains); the research criterion of the retrofit says: Cross.B must not FAIL, CANNOT_RUN is reported and is not a pass; the pilot of ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB models the chains in ONE chapter (chapter 6); carrying the model to the other 24 chapters is a further item, not part of this iteration. (c) The execution checks of eleven chapters fail on this machine for reasons of the environment (installed packages, services, timing): a claim is made reproducible by an isolated environment the data module builds itself, or it is reported as printed (FAIL) and the criterion is NOT MET; no claim is weakened to pass, and a skip is not a pass. (d) The end of Iter_20 is the proposed end of seven days (G9); a rebaseline is an owner decision. 16 chapters at 14.5 h are 232 h, and the pilot 8.5 h: with at most three executors at once and the page tests serial on two cores the plan does not promise that all sixteen chapters finish inside it; a chapter that is not Done at the review is said to be not Done and is carried by the change route, not hidden. (e) The Deck and Page cases of the chapter check were not run for chapters 10 to 25. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog stage is revised once more (G125 route 2). Iter_20 gets its start (the planning ceremony), its end (seven days, G9), its sprint goal, the sixteen stories of chapters 10 to 25 (Ready, scored, six tasks each: 96 tasks) and the Cross.B story (Ready, scored, four tasks): 100 tasks; the story ex:ST_Plan_Remaining is withdrawn (Cancelled) on the measurement of fact 1; the retrofit criterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit is restated for these chapters and ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch20 is added; ex:AC2F_CrossB is planned as a pilot on chapter 6; the exclusion ex:Excl2_NoRebuild is lifted for the NEW files of chapters 10 to 25 and the pilot only. RE-RANKING of the open items (WSJF: business value 20; time criticality 20 for chapter 10 down to 5 for chapter 25, the owner's order of chapters; risk reduction = the deck-standard elements measured failing + 2 for Stage 4 never run (no page ABox) + 1 where the chapter check fails on the execution checks; job size 14.5 h): the order is chapter 10, 11, ..., 25; inside a chapter the order of the dependencies (deck, deck control, page, research set and page ABox, research control, page control); the Cross.B pilot after chapter 25 (business value 8, time criticality 4, risk reduction 1, job size 8.5 h). BATCHES (the plan of the controller, not a promise): at most THREE executor sessions at once; the next startable task of the highest-ranked chapter takes a free place; deck builds and research sets run side by side, page builds one at a time (they hold the page-test lock for hours), the controller's page tests wait in the same queue; the Cross.B pilot takes a place only when no higher-ranked task can start. Not in the plan: a rebaseline, a waiver, an edit of a gate or test, a new metric." .

ex:Revision_Lineage2_Backlog11 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the second lineage from the Backlog stage: Iteration 20 planned for the retrofit of chapters 10 to 25 and the Cross.B pilot"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR2_Iter20, ex:IA2_Iter20 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Direction of the course coordinator, 2026-10-25, recorded as relayed: the Iteration 19 close is accepted; run the Iteration 20 change route now without waiting for the owner: check the stories against the verified gaps, change request and impact assessment, re-rank in the owner's order, generate the briefs from the current generator with the lessons of Iteration 19 folded in (new tool files from the start, the page-ABox builder v1_1_13, the page-ABox version above the old one, the story-layout probe on every story, the first-line error scan on manifests, the executor's own probe as strict as the controller's); plan the batches so that at most three executors run at once (two cores; the serial page-test lock was the bottleneck of Iteration 19; decks and research in parallel, page tests the only serial part). The owner's decision of Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul (13:06 UTC) (ex:CR2_Priority3), recorded as relayed, is the release: after chapters 7, 8 and 9, return to ALL chapters (chapters 1 to 5 are done and controlled), and after that build all remaining chapters. Stories become Ready with scores and tasks, a criterion is added and another restated, a story is withdrawn: the closed Backlog stage's digest moves (G117, G125 route 2): a StageRevision from the Backlog stage, never from the Mission; the change request CR2_Iter20 and the impact assessment IA2_Iter20 were recorded first. This version retracts the Backlog output Out2_BacklogR10 and rebuilds nothing; the next version closes the Backlog stage again as Out2_BacklogR11 and re-admits every item without re-dating any; a third version fills the commit. The retracted output and its digest stay as history (L-112)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR10 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "1acb5c3" .
ex:Out2_BacklogR10 backlog:outputRetracted true .


ex:TK_Ret_Ch10_Deck_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the deck of chapter 10 (Reading and Writing Files) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ret_Ch10_Deck_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the deck of chapter 10 (Reading and Writing Files) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_20 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T10:03:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T10:27:36"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck10, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck10_0, ex:Ev2_CtlFile_deck10_1 ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_DeckCheck ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: build the deck of chapter 10 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research (03-materials/ch10/rdodi, the newest research) and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard; the new deck goes to 03-materials/ch10/ named like the decks of chapters 6 to 9: `03-materials/ch10/SEN0414_Ch10_ReadingWritingFiles_3e_v2_0_0.pptx`; the earlier chapter 10 deck lives in 08-tooling/ch10-deck/ and stays where it is. The owner's teaching-material rules: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs (no text box over 30 words); explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes (at most 60 words); one smooth colour scheme; dividers that name their concepts with a line of meaning and a visual; coverage of the research concepts not below 90 percent. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch10/page/chapter_code_ch10_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code exactly as on the slide, the slide number, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file in 08-tooling/ch10-deck; the checker is the independent TK_Std_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch10; estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control. DECK LESSONS: (a) FIRST-LINE ERROR SCAN: the page template draws a result as a chart or a table, but an output whose FIRST line matches ^(\\w*Error|Traceback|Stopped after) is drawn as text and the page test 9.37.0 (P2) then fails that example for want of a visual (six decks of chapters 1, 3 and 4 had to be repaired for this). Write every example whose purpose is to raise an error so that it prints an ordinary line FIRST (a heading line such as 'Result: ...' or the value before the error), and run `python3 08-tooling/sen0414_manifest_error_first_scan_v1_0_0.py 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json` - it must print RESULT: PASS - before you report. (b) The examples of the manifest run under Python 3.13 (the controller's interpreter for them) and print exactly the recorded result: run all of them and compare, and say how you did. (c) Story pictures are real pictures with a recorded licence, embedded in the deck; every story names who, what, when, where, why and how and has a live link. (d) The deck and its manifest are final when you report: the page task copies the manifest; a later deck repair costs a new deck, a new manifest and a rebuilt page. (e) Run the overlap check and fix every finding in a NEW deck version; report CLEAN or the findings as printed. Planned session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch10. Estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch10_Deck_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 10 (Reading and Writing Files) as it stands (measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent): research 03-materials/ch10/rdodi (document 1_0_1, domain TBox 1_0_0, ABox 1_0_0, SHACL 1_0_0, research 1_0_0); data module sen0414_ch10_rdodi_data_v1_0_1.py; corpus sen0414_ch10_corpus_base_v1_0_0.py; stories sen0414_ch10_stories_v1_0_0.py; the earlier deck is sen0414_ch10_deck_v1_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v1_0_0.py) - it lives in 08-tooling/ch10-deck/, NOT in 03-materials, and stays there; newest page sen0414_ch10_page_v9_28_0.html; page ABox: NONE (the first page ABox of this chapter is built by the research task); chapter-code manifest: none. The deck standard check v1_0_0 on the earlier deck prints 7 failing elements (D1,D2,D3,D4,D11,D5,D7; M1 and D10 not measured) and the overlap check ends FINDINGS (2 findings). The chapter check Research/Ch10 ends PASS: the gates end OVERALL: PASS, Stage 4 is not run (no page ABox exists), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN; the execution checks of the data module end exit 0 with 0 MISMATCH line(s) (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_Ch10.log: read it first - the claims that print a mismatch here depend on what is installed on this machine or on a service). LESSONS OF ITERATION 19 (the rules of this iteration): (1) A committed file is never edited - and that includes your OWN tool scripts, builders, data modules, test drivers and logs: every new version of any of them is a NEW file with a new version number FROM THE FIRST SAVE (do not save vX, commit it and then edit it; the controller found two such in-place edits by git and they were disclosed in the register); only a file you have not yet committed may be regenerated. (2) Report negative results first and as printed; a skip is not a pass; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is not a pass. (3) The machine has two cores shared by up to three executors: every browser test runs under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`; no build or corpus run beside a browser test of yours; a timing-sensitive check can fail under load - say so, rerun on a quiet machine, keep the failing log. (4) Everything you cite in your report is a commit you made and a file that exists; the controller re-runs every claim, so a report that says more than the files show is NOT MET." .

