    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: Build the page of chapter 12 as a NEW file with a new page version (the new page is **v9_95_0**: `03-materials/ch12/page/sen0414_ch12_page_v9_95_0.html`, above the chapter's newest page sen0414_ch12_page_v9_28_0.html; the pages of chapters 1 to 9 are v9_90_0 to v9_92_0) on the template 9.52.2 (08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_2.html) with the page builder v4_18_1 (08-tooling/sen0414_page_build_v4_18_1.py) and the page-data builder v2_25_0 (state how you passed the template), from the chapter research, the deck's lecture export and stories, and the deck's chapter-code manifest. Run the page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 (the runner sen0414_page_test_run_v1_1_0.py; PAGE_TEST_FILE=sen0414_page_test_v9_37_0.py for 9.37.0), serially, store the result as a new test_results file in 08-tooling/ch12-page, and run the chapter check Page/Ch12 if it has the case for the chapter (the controller does not rely on it; report what it prints). PAGE STANDARD (checked by the page test 9.37.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I20-page-ch12; estimated 3.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the deck of the chapter is controlled. PAGE LESSONS: (a) STORY LAYOUT, measured on EVERY story: the photograph of a story is lower than the viewport and the narrative paragraph begins within the first screen of the story. Run `flock /tmp/page_test.lock python3 08-tooling/sen0414_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py PAGE.html 08-tooling/chNN-page/story_layout_YOUR_RUN.log` on your page: it checks every story card at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, the FIRST story as the reader sees it when the Stories tab opens (no scrolling), the later ones with the card scrolled to the top. It is the controller's rule; your own probe must be at least as strict - a looser rule of your own does not count, a stricter one is welcome. Portrait photographs (a head and shoulders) must be cropped or sized so that they do not fill the phone screen. (b) The first-line error scan of the manifest (`sen0414_manifest_error_first_scan_v1_0_0.py`, see the deck lesson) must print PASS on the manifest you build from; if it does not, STOP and report - the deck is repaired by a new deck version and a new manifest, never by editing. (c) The Lab / Playground examples pane takes its examples from a NEW examples file made FROM THE MANIFEST (same code, same order), not from an older examples file. (d) The page file names: `03-materials/chNN/page/sen0414_chNN_page_v9_95_0.html` and the page inputs under the v9_95_0 name; if you need another version name, STOP and report. (e) Run page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 on the page, serially under the lock, and keep every log, the failing ones too. Planned session SEN0414-I20-page-ch12. Estimated 3.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the deck of the chapter is controlled." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch12_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 12 (Command Line Programs) as it stands (measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent): research 03-materials/ch12/rdodi (document 1_0_2, domain TBox 1_0_2, ABox 1_0_2, SHACL 1_0_2, research 1_0_2); data module sen0414_ch12_rdodi_data_v1_0_2.py; corpus sen0414_ch12_corpus_base_v1_0_0.py; stories sen0414_ch12_stories_v1_0_0.py; the earlier deck is sen0414_ch12_deck_v1_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v1_0_0.py) - it lives in 08-tooling/ch12-deck/, NOT in 03-materials, and stays there; newest page sen0414_ch12_page_v9_28_0.html; page ABox: NONE (the first page ABox of this chapter is built by the research task); chapter-code manifest: none. The deck standard check v1_0_0 on the earlier deck prints 8 failing elements (D1,D2,D3,D4,D11,D5,D7,D12; M1 and D10 not measured) and the overlap check ends CLEAN (0 findings). The chapter check Research/Ch12 ends PASS: the gates end OVERALL: PASS, Stage 4 is not run (no page ABox exists), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN; the execution checks of the data module end exit 0 with 0 MISMATCH line(s) (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_Ch12.log: read it first - the claims that print a mismatch here depend on what is installed on this machine or on a service). LESSONS OF ITERATION 19 (the rules of this iteration): (1) A committed file is never edited - and that includes your OWN tool scripts, builders, data modules, test drivers and logs: every new version of any of them is a NEW file with a new version number FROM THE FIRST SAVE (do not save vX, commit it and then edit it; the controller found two such in-place edits by git and they were disclosed in the register); only a file you have not yet committed may be regenerated. (2) Report negative results first and as printed; a skip is not a pass; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is not a pass. (3) The machine has two cores shared by up to three executors: every browser test runs under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`; no build or corpus run beside a browser test of yours; a timing-sensitive check can fail under load - say so, rerun on a quiet machine, keep the failing log. (4) Everything you cite in your report is a commit you made and a file that exists; the controller re-runs every claim, so a report that says more than the files show is NOT MET." .

