    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the research set of chapter 14 (Excel Spreadsheets) pass the chapter check Research/Ch14, with its FIRST page ABox, which describes the NEW page. Read the criterion (ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch20) and the precedents first: the chapters 1 to 5 of Iteration 19 (research task commits of chapters 2 to 5: `git log --oneline -- 03-materials/ch05/rdodi 03-materials/ch05/page 08-tooling/ch05-research`; the comparison tools 08-tooling/sen0414_ch0N_page_abox_compare_v1_0_0.py; the data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch05_rdodi_data_v1_3_0.py and its restore script), chapter 6 (data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_2_0.py, page ABox 03-materials/ch06/page/sen0414_ch06_page_abox_v1_4_0.ttl) and chapter 7 (data module v1_3_0, how a data module is made from a corpus). THE DIFFERENCE FROM CHAPTERS 1 TO 5: this chapter has no page ABox yet (the gates' Stage 4 and Cross.B have never run for it); its research files may already pass (see the facts) - then they are NOT rebuilt - or its execution checks fail on this machine (see the facts and the log): then a NEW data version and NEW files are needed. Nothing is invented: content comes from the book's chapter, the deck, the page and the existing files. A committed file is never edited. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is reported as such and is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores shared by up to three executors: no build beside a browser test. Planned session SEN0414-I20-research-ch14; estimated 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the page of the chapter is controlled (the page ABox describes the new page). RESEARCH LESSONS: (a) The page-ABox builder is `08-tooling/sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_13.py`; it knows every visual kind of chapters 1 to 9. If it stops on a visual kind of YOUR page, write `sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_14.py` as a NEW file over v1_1_13 (never edit v1_1_13) and say which kind. (b) NAME THE PAGE ABOX `03-materials/chNN/page/sen0414_chNN_page_abox_v9_95_0.ttl`: the gate ranks page ABoxes by version, and the chapter check must pick the one that describes the new page. No older page ABox exists for this chapter; the name keeps that true for the next version too. (c) COMPARE old and new with a script of your own (a NEW tool file) before you report, and list every difference with its reason: individuals, classes, links, sources, labels. In chapters 1 to 5 the new page showed static examples where the old widgets had step-through primitives and some widgets lost links; each such loss was stated and judged. State yours. (d) The execution checks of this chapter fail on the controller's machine today (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_ChNN.log): read the mismatches first. A claim whose output depends on an installed package, a service, the clock or the machine's load must be made reproducible - for example by running it in an isolated virtual environment that the data module builds itself, with a stated package version, or with a wide time limit - or be reported as printed; do not weaken the claim, do not delete it, do not skip it. A signal-timing claim that waits 0.3 s and demands an answer in 3 s fails under load: use limits that load cannot break. (e) The controller runs the chapter check on its machine with the python3.14 on its path; your claims must pass there, under the load of other sessions. Planned session SEN0414-I20-research-ch14. Estimated 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the page of the chapter is controlled (the page ABox describes the new page); the research set itself may be prepared earlier but its page ABox is built last." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch14_Research backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 14 (Excel Spreadsheets) as it stands (measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent): research 03-materials/ch14/rdodi (document 1_0_2, domain TBox 1_0_2, ABox 1_0_2, SHACL 1_0_2, research 1_0_2); data module sen0414_ch14_rdodi_data_v1_0_2.py; corpus sen0414_ch14_corpus_base_v1_0_0.py; stories sen0414_ch14_stories_v1_0_0.py; the earlier deck is sen0414_ch14_deck_v1_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v1_0_0.py) - it lives in 08-tooling/ch14-deck/, NOT in 03-materials, and stays there; newest page sen0414_ch14_page_v9_29_0.html; page ABox: NONE (the first page ABox of this chapter is built by the research task); chapter-code manifest: none. The deck standard check v1_0_0 on the earlier deck prints 7 failing elements (D1,D2,D3,D4,D11,D5,D7; M1 and D10 not measured) and the overlap check ends CLEAN (0 findings). The chapter check Research/Ch14 ends FAIL: the gates end OVERALL: PASS, Stage 4 is not run (no page ABox exists), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN; the execution checks of the data module end exit 1 with 2 MISMATCH line(s) (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_Ch14.log: read it first - the claims that print a mismatch here depend on what is installed on this machine or on a service). LESSONS OF ITERATION 19 (the rules of this iteration): (1) A committed file is never edited - and that includes your OWN tool scripts, builders, data modules, test drivers and logs: every new version of any of them is a NEW file with a new version number FROM THE FIRST SAVE (do not save vX, commit it and then edit it; the controller found two such in-place edits by git and they were disclosed in the register); only a file you have not yet committed may be regenerated. (2) Report negative results first and as printed; a skip is not a pass; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is not a pass. (3) The machine has two cores shared by up to three executors: every browser test runs under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`; no build or corpus run beside a browser test of yours; a timing-sensitive check can fail under load - say so, rerun on a quiet machine, keep the failing log. (4) Everything you cite in your report is a commit you made and a file that exists; the controller re-runs every claim, so a report that says more than the files show is NOT MET." .

