    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the research set of chapter 15 (Google Sheets) pass the chapter check Research/Ch15, with its FIRST page ABox, which describes the NEW page. Read the criterion (ex:AC2F_RetrofitResearch20) and the precedents first: the chapters 1 to 5 of Iteration 19 (research task commits of chapters 2 to 5: `git log --oneline -- 03-materials/ch05/rdodi 03-materials/ch05/page 08-tooling/ch05-research`; the comparison tools 08-tooling/sen0414_ch0N_page_abox_compare_v1_0_0.py; the data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch05_rdodi_data_v1_3_0.py and its restore script), chapter 6 (data module 08-tooling/sen0414_ch06_rdodi_data_v2_2_0.py, page ABox 03-materials/ch06/page/sen0414_ch06_page_abox_v1_4_0.ttl) and chapter 7 (data module v1_3_0, how a data module is made from a corpus). THE DIFFERENCE FROM CHAPTERS 1 TO 5: this chapter has no page ABox yet (the gates' Stage 4 and Cross.B have never run for it); its research files may already pass (see the facts) - then they are NOT rebuilt - or its execution checks fail on this machine (see the facts and the log): then a NEW data version and NEW files are needed. Nothing is invented: content comes from the book's chapter, the deck, the page and the existing files. A committed file is never edited. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is reported as such and is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores shared by up to three executors: no build beside a browser test. Planned session SEN0414-I20-research-ch15; estimated 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the page of the chapter is controlled (the page ABox describes the new page). RESEARCH LESSONS: (a) The page-ABox builder is `08-tooling/sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_13.py`; it knows every visual kind of chapters 1 to 9. If it stops on a visual kind of YOUR page, write `sen0414_page_abox_build_v1_1_14.py` as a NEW file over v1_1_13 (never edit v1_1_13) and say which kind. (b) NAME THE PAGE ABOX `03-materials/chNN/page/sen0414_chNN_page_abox_v9_95_0.ttl`: the gate ranks page ABoxes by version, and the chapter check must pick the one that describes the new page. No older page ABox exists for this chapter; the name keeps that true for the next version too. (c) COMPARE old and new with a script of your own (a NEW tool file) before you report, and list every difference with its reason: individuals, classes, links, sources, labels. In chapters 1 to 5 the new page showed static examples where the old widgets had step-through primitives and some widgets lost links; each such loss was stated and judged. State yours. (d) The execution checks of this chapter fail on the controller's machine today (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_ChNN.log): read the mismatches first. A claim whose output depends on an installed package, a service, the clock or the machine's load must be made reproducible - for example by running it in an isolated virtual environment that the data module builds itself, with a stated package version, or with a wide time limit - or be reported as printed; do not weaken the claim, do not delete it, do not skip it. A signal-timing claim that waits 0.3 s and demands an answer in 3 s fails under load: use limits that load cannot break. (e) The controller runs the chapter check on its machine with the python3.14 on its path; your claims must pass there, under the load of other sessions. Planned session SEN0414-I20-research-ch15. Estimated 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts when the page of the chapter is controlled (the page ABox describes the new page); the research set itself may be prepared earlier but its page ABox is built last." .
