ex:Score30_ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch17 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ;
    backlog:hasScoreValue "2.97"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:scoredAt "2026-10-25T09:46:42"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:isAveragedFromMembers false ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "WSJF = (business value 20 + time criticality 13 + risk reduction 10) / job size 14.5 h = 2.97. Inputs from observable facts: job size is the sum of the story's task estimates in this register (Deck_Build 5.0 h, Deck_Verify 0.5 h, Page_Build 3.5 h, Research 4.0 h, Research_Verify 0.5 h, Page_Verify 1.0 h); time criticality 13 = place 8 in the owner's order of chapters of Iteration 20 (20 = chapter 10, 5 = chapter 25); risk reduction 10 = the deck-standard elements measured failing (7) + 2 for Stage 4 never run (no page ABox) + 1 where the chapter check fails on the execution checks (measured 2026-10-25 UTC). Scored on 2026-10-25T09:46:42 UTC at the planning of Iteration 20 (ex:CR2_Iter20); the earlier planned-and-unscored state is history." .
ex:ST_Plan_Retrofit_Ch17 backlog:hasAuditNote "PLANNED INTO ITERATION 20 on 2026-10-25T09:46:42 UTC (ex:CR2_Iter20, planning ceremony ex:PC2_Iter_20): Ready, scored, decomposed into six tasks (deck build, deck verify, page build, research set and page ABox, research verify, page verify). CHAPTER 17 (PDF and Word Documents) as it stands (measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent): research 03-materials/ch17/rdodi (document 1_0_2, domain TBox 1_0_2, ABox 1_0_2, SHACL 1_0_2, research 1_0_2); data module sen0414_ch17_rdodi_data_v1_0_2.py; corpus sen0414_ch17_corpus_base_v1_0_0.py; stories sen0414_ch17_stories_v1_0_0.py; the earlier deck is sen0414_ch17_deck_v1_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v1_0_0.py) - it lives in 08-tooling/ch17-deck/, NOT in 03-materials, and stays there; newest page sen0414_ch17_page_v9_32_0.html; page ABox: NONE (the first page ABox of this chapter is built by the research task); chapter-code manifest: none. The deck standard check v1_0_0 on the earlier deck prints 7 failing elements (D1,D2,D3,D4,D11,D5,D7; M1 and D10 not measured) and the overlap check ends CLEAN (0 findings). The chapter check Research/Ch17 ends FAIL: the gates end OVERALL: PASS, Stage 4 is not run (no page ABox exists), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN; the execution checks of the data module end exit 1 with 4 MISMATCH line(s) (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_Ch17.log: read it first - the claims that print a mismatch here depend on what is installed on this machine or on a service). GAPS SAID OPENLY: (a) the metrics Met2_StdDecks and Met2_StdPages count the decks and pages of chapters 6, 7 and 8 (target 3) and read 3 and 3; the retrofit of chapters 10 to 25 moves no number of them, as that of chapters 1 to 5 did not (ex:Finding2_Iter19_MetricScope); widening them is the Owner's decision and no rebaseline is written; the review of Iteration 20 reports the chapters as readings in the method text. (b) Cross.B of the research gates cannot run in any chapter (0 hybrid chains); the research criterion of the retrofit says: Cross.B must not FAIL, CANNOT_RUN is reported and is not a pass; the pilot of ex:ST_Plan_Gap_CrossB models the chains in ONE chapter (chapter 6); carrying the model to the other 24 chapters is a further item, not part of this iteration. (c) The execution checks of eleven chapters fail on this machine for reasons of the environment (installed packages, services, timing): a claim is made reproducible by an isolated environment the data module builds itself, or it is reported as printed (FAIL) and the criterion is NOT MET; no claim is weakened to pass, and a skip is not a pass. (d) The end of Iter_20 is the proposed end of seven days (G9); a rebaseline is an owner decision. 16 chapters at 14.5 h are 232 h, and the pilot 8.5 h: with at most three executors at once and the page tests serial on two cores the plan does not promise that all sixteen chapters finish inside it; a chapter that is not Done at the review is said to be not Done and is carried by the change route, not hidden. (e) The Deck and Page cases of the chapter check were not run for chapters 10 to 25. No executor has started; work begun is recorded at the real start of each executor session." .

ex:TK_Ret_Ch18_Deck_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the deck of chapter 18 (CSV, JSON and XML Files) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ret_Ch18_Deck_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the deck of chapter 18 (CSV, JSON and XML Files) against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_20 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out2_BacklogR11 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-26T12:18:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Std_DeckCheck ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RETROFIT: build the deck of chapter 18 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research (03-materials/ch18/rdodi, the newest research) and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard; the new deck goes to 03-materials/ch18/ named like the decks of chapters 6 to 9: `03-materials/ch18/SEN0414_Ch18_CSVJSONXML_3e_v2_0_0.pptx`; the earlier chapter 18 deck lives in 08-tooling/ch18-deck/ and stays where it is. The owner's teaching-material rules: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs (no text box over 30 words); explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes (at most 60 words); one smooth colour scheme; dividers that name their concepts with a line of meaning and a visual; coverage of the research concepts not below 90 percent. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. THE OWNER'S CENTRAL REQUIREMENT: the code on the slides appears exactly, in the same order, in the chapter-code tab of the page, and runs there. The manifest 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json is written from the deck (order, name, code, slide number, expected result); the deck check proves the manifest equals the deck's code boxes (text and order) and the page test proves the tab equals the manifest (names, order, code) and that each example runs and shows its result. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch18/page/chapter_code_ch18_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code exactly as on the slide, the slide number, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file in 08-tooling/ch18-deck; the checker is the independent TK_Std_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch18; estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control. DECK LESSONS: (a) FIRST-LINE ERROR SCAN: the page template draws a result as a chart or a table, but an output whose FIRST line matches ^(\\w*Error|Traceback|Stopped after) is drawn as text and the page test 9.37.0 (P2) then fails that example for want of a visual (six decks of chapters 1, 3 and 4 had to be repaired for this). Write every example whose purpose is to raise an error so that it prints an ordinary line FIRST (a heading line such as 'Result: ...' or the value before the error), and run `python3 08-tooling/sen0414_manifest_error_first_scan_v1_0_0.py 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v1_0_0.json` - it must print RESULT: PASS - before you report. (b) The examples of the manifest run under Python 3.13 (the controller's interpreter for them) and print exactly the recorded result: run all of them and compare, and say how you did. (c) Story pictures are real pictures with a recorded licence, embedded in the deck; every story names who, what, when, where, why and how and has a live link. (d) The deck and its manifest are final when you report: the page task copies the manifest; a later deck repair costs a new deck, a new manifest and a rebuilt page. (e) Run the overlap check and fix every finding in a NEW deck version; report CLEAN or the findings as printed. Planned session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch18. Estimated 5.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun). Starts first in the chapter: the later tasks depend on its control." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch18_Deck_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Facts for this task, measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent: CHAPTER 18 (CSV, JSON and XML Files) as it stands (measured 2026-10-25 UTC by the lineage agent): research 03-materials/ch18/rdodi (document 1_0_2, domain TBox 1_0_2, ABox 1_0_2, SHACL 1_0_2, research 1_0_2); data module sen0414_ch18_rdodi_data_v1_0_2.py; corpus sen0414_ch18_corpus_base_v1_0_0.py; stories sen0414_ch18_stories_v1_0_0.py; the earlier deck is sen0414_ch18_deck_v1_0_0.pptx (builder deck_build_v1_0_0.py) - it lives in 08-tooling/ch18-deck/, NOT in 03-materials, and stays there; newest page sen0414_ch18_page_v9_33_0.html; page ABox: NONE (the first page ABox of this chapter is built by the research task); chapter-code manifest: none. The deck standard check v1_0_0 on the earlier deck prints 7 failing elements (D1,D2,D3,D4,D11,D5,D7; M1 and D10 not measured) and the overlap check ends CLEAN (0 findings). The chapter check Research/Ch18 ends FAIL: the gates end OVERALL: PASS, Stage 4 is not run (no page ABox exists), Cross.B CANNOT_RUN; the execution checks of the data module end exit 1 with 1 MISMATCH line(s) (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/pre_Research_Ch18.log: read it first - the claims that print a mismatch here depend on what is installed on this machine or on a service). LESSONS OF ITERATION 19 (the rules of this iteration): (1) A committed file is never edited - and that includes your OWN tool scripts, builders, data modules, test drivers and logs: every new version of any of them is a NEW file with a new version number FROM THE FIRST SAVE (do not save vX, commit it and then edit it; the controller found two such in-place edits by git and they were disclosed in the register); only a file you have not yet committed may be regenerated. (2) Report negative results first and as printed; a skip is not a pass; Cross.B CANNOT_RUN is not a pass. (3) The machine has two cores shared by up to three executors: every browser test runs under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`; no build or corpus run beside a browser test of yours; a timing-sensitive check can fail under load - say so, rerun on a quiet machine, keep the failing log. (4) Everything you cite in your report is a commit you made and a file that exists; the controller re-runs every claim, so a report that says more than the files show is NOT MET." .

