ex:TK_Ret_Ch10_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Added at the control of the chapter 10 deck (register 2.239.0), recorded 2026-10-25 UTC: (1) the story 4 slide of the deck (slide 31) is titled 'JSON was written up in 2001' and gives 12 November 2002 for json.org, which reads as two dates; the page's story text for it must say the facts plainly (the first JSON message in 2001, json.org in 2002) and must not copy the ambiguity; the deck is NOT changed (a deck change would be a new deck and a rebuilt manifest, out of proportion). (2) Every link on the page is re-verified by the executor; the executor states which it could not reach. This note was passed to the executor by the coordinator in the executor prompt, not in the brief (the brief file is unchanged, SHA-256 as recorded at work begun)." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch11_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "Added at the control of the chapter 11 deck (register 2.240.0), recorded 2026-10-25 UTC, for the executor of this task: the YouTube link of the chapter 11 resources slide (Corey Schafer, ZIP files) answered 429 to the deck executor's check; the oEmbed answer shows the video exists. Re-check the link when you build the page, say what you got, and do not drop it without a stated reason. Story 4 and the other stories: state every date plainly." .

ex:Ev2_Ctl_page10 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 10 page (03-materials/ch10/page/sen0414_ch10_page_v9_95_0.html, rebuilt on the chapter-code manifest 1_0_0 of the new deck, template 9.52.2, builder 4.18.1, page-data builder 2.25.0; commits 9958930 and e879c6d of the executor session SEN0414-I20-page-ch10; the earlier page v9_28_0 stays as committed): the controller's own serial runs under the shared lock - page test 9.37.0 through the runner v1_1_0 on the page: exit 0, 402 features passed, 0 failed, widgets 59 and 59, P2 examples, P11 and P12 pass, none skipped; page test 9.34.0 on the page: 376 passed, 0 failed, and on the earlier page v9_28_0: 376 passed, 0 failed (widgets 59 and 59, not below, none skipped); the chapter check Page/Ch10 run by the controller under the lock: PASS (the executor's run crashed because it was made without the lock); the chapter-code tab data equals the manifest (18 of 18, order, names, code), which equals the deck's code boxes (M1 18 of 18); the Chapter examples pane equals the manifest (18 of 18, observation); the first-line error scan of the manifest PASS (0 of 18); the four story pictures embedded as data URIs; the story-layout probe v1_0_0 (the one rule) passes for all four stories at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844 (12 of 12; the first story's text begins at 719 of 768 px on the desktop and 837 of 844 px at phone width, which meets the rule only barely and is said here); no committed file modified since the register commit that planned Iteration 20, everything committed; the controller looked at the Start, Stories and Chapter code views at 1366 and 390 px: legible, the code runs from the tab. THE DATE WORDING (the note of the deck control): the page's story about JSON says 'the quoted, minimal format he wrote up in 2001 became JSON; he opened json.org on 12 November 2002' - two events, each dated once, from the cited Wikipedia article (2001 for the format, 12 November 2002 for json.org); the controller reads it as plain and exact, not as a conflict, so NO wording change, no new stories file and no new page are needed (a change route is not opened); the note called it story 4, it is story 3 of the page. Under load the controller's FIRST runs of 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 failed (a browser tab crash and a click timeout while other sessions' tests ran on the two cores; logs p37_ch10_t37_run1_FAIL_crash_under_load.log and p37_ch10_t34_run1_FAIL_timeout_under_load.log are kept); the reruns on a quieter machine pass; no test, threshold or timeout was changed."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit ;
