Disclosures of the executor, judged: the pip story shows a small terminal screenshot (Cedar101, CC BY-SA 3.0) and the Norton story a Midnight Commander screenshot (GPL), both captioned as screenshots - accepted for Norton (the figure of the chapter itself); the pip picture is small and dark, so its text is not readable on the slide - accepted as a real picture with a licence, noted as the weakest picture of the deck, the criterion asks for a real picture and not for a portrait of Ian Bicking; the McIlroy and Ritchie photographs carry the same artist and credit (Denise Panyik-Dale, CC BY 2.0, one Flickr source) - the controller could not reach the Commons file pages (the fetch was refused, the API call returned no usable answer), so the credit is NOT independently verified by the controller and is recorded as the executor's reading of the Commons metadata. Not repeated by the controller: a Pyodide run of the manifest (only the Python 3.13 run was repeated); the executor's Pyodide claim stands as the executor's.. Evidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck12, verified by backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0." .
