ex:TK_Ret_Ch12_Deck_Verify backlog:hasAuditNote "Controlled by the lineage agent on 2026-10-25T12:45:05 UTC: the chapter 12 deck (03-materials/ch12/SEN0414_Ch12_CommandLinePrograms_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 48 slides, 23 examples, 4 stories, with the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch12/page/chapter_code_ch12_v1_0_0.json; commit 289ce81 of the executor session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch12; the earlier deck 08-tooling/ch12-deck/sen0414_ch12_deck_v1_0_0.pptx stays as committed): the controller's own re-runs - the deck standard check v1_0_0 prints SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 including M1 (manifest equals the deck's code boxes, text and order, 23 of 23), the overlap check v1_0_0 ends CLEAN (0 findings), the first-line error scan of the manifest ends PASS (0 of 23), the 23 examples run now under Python 3.13.16 in a fresh interpreter print exactly the recorded result, no committed file of the chapter is modified since the register commit that planned Iteration 20 (18 files added), everything is committed; the 4 story pictures (pip, McIlroy, Midnight Commander, Ritchie) cover the 4 story slides with a licence record in story_images_v2_0_0.json. A first run of control script v1_0_0 failed only its picture assertion, because it required my own file names (photo_*, ASSETS_PROVENANCE_*.md) and the executor used image_* names and a JSON record; the criterion does not name the files, so the assertion was rewritten as a new file v1_1_0 and the first-run log is not kept as a verdict. The controller rendered all 48 slides and read a selection (title, analogy table, venv, argv with chart, chr and os.system, launcher table, clipboard recorder, resources) and the four story slides: legible, numbered, explanation beside each listing, 5N1K in all four stories. Links: 16 of the 17 hyperlinks answered 200 to the controller; the Wikipedia Pipeline (Unix) page answered 429 (rate limit; the page exists and is the READ link of the McIlroy story) - a live-link item to re-check, not a gate failure. Disclosures of the executor, judged: the pip story shows a small terminal screenshot (Cedar101, CC BY-SA 3.0) and the Norton story a Midnight Commander screenshot (GPL), both captioned as screenshots - accepted for Norton (the figure of the chapter itself); the pip picture is small and dark, so its text is not readable on the slide - accepted as a real picture with a licence, noted as the weakest picture of the deck, the criterion asks for a real picture and not for a portrait of Ian Bicking; the McIlroy and Ritchie photographs carry the same artist and credit (Denise Panyik-Dale, CC BY 2.0, one Flickr source) - the controller could not reach the Commons file pages (the fetch was refused, the API call returned no usable answer), so the credit is NOT independently verified by the controller and is recorded as the executor's reading of the Commons metadata. Not repeated by the controller: a Pyodide run of the manifest (only the Python 3.13 run was repeated); the executor's Pyodide claim stands as the executor's.. Evidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck12, verified by backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0." .
