ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck13 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 13 deck (03-materials/ch13/SEN0414_Ch13_WebScraping_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 51 slides, 24 examples, 7 native charts, 6 stories, with the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch13/page/chapter_code_ch13_v1_0_0.json; commit 8827ca1 of the executor session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch13; the earlier deck 08-tooling/ch13-deck/sen0414_ch13_deck_v1_0_0.pptx stays as committed): the controller's own re-runs - the deck standard check v1_0_0 prints SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 including M1 (24 of 24), the overlap check ends CLEAN (0 findings), the first-line error scan of the manifest ends PASS, the 24 examples run now under Python 3.13.16 print exactly the recorded result, no committed file of the chapter is modified since the register commit that planned Iteration 20 (21 files added), everything is committed, the 6 story pictures cover the 6 story slides with a licence or status record in ASSETS_PROVENANCE_v1_0_0.md and the two story_images JSON files (control script v1_2_0: the first run of v1_1_0 failed only because its file pattern did not include the second JSON file story_images_other_v2_0_0.json; a new file, not an edit); all 19 hyperlinks answered 200 to the controller; the controller rendered all 51 slides and read the six story slides (5N1K in each, READ link on each). Not repeated by the controller: the executor's Pyodide 0.28.2 run of the 24 examples (the executor's claim stands as the executor's). Disclosures of the executor, judged: (1) the Gray story (slide 13) shows The First Web Server (CERN, CC BY 2.0, asvensson via Flickr), not Matthew Gray - a real photograph of the real object the story is about, captioned openly as not Gray's machine: accepted as a stand-in; (2) the Koster story (slide 11) shows a rendering the executor drew of the live pypi.org/robots.txt fetched 2026-10-25, not the 1994 file, captioned as drawn for this deck: it is a drawing, not a found picture, and the owner's rule asks for real pictures, not invented ones; it is real content (a real robots.txt) and says openly what it is, so it is accepted for delivery but is an OPEN OWNER CONTENT DECISION, recorded beside chapter 2, to be replaced by a real picture (a photograph of Koster or a capture of the 1994 file) once a source is reachable; (3) Richardson picture is Tenniel's Mock Turtle, public domain by age, taken from crummy.com with no licence stated for the file - accepted; Selenium and Playwright logos are the projects' own marks with Apache-2.0 on the project repositories (the trademarks belong to their owners) - accepted; Reitz photograph CC BY 3.0 (Nils Pascal Illenseer) - accepted; the examples use standard-library stand-ins for Requests, Beautiful Soup, Selenium and Playwright, named on each slide - accepted (the examples run offline and say so); the cause of the stand-ins was Wikimedia answering 429 for hours, and the picture fetch script was never committed - noted as a gap in the executor's record (the pictures and their records are committed, the means of getting them is not); the Real Python link (403) and a pyvideo link (404) were not used. The page test and the story probe belong to the page task."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit ;
