ex:TK_Ret_Ch11_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "NOT MET on the first report, found by the controller on 2026-10-25T14:06:42 UTC with its own run of the story-layout probe v1_0_0 under the lock on page v9_95_0 (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/probe_ch11_v9_95_0.log): 'FAIL story 2 at 390x844: photo height 442 of 844, first text 857.42', all other 11 lines PASS. Story 2 is Mark Adler, a portrait photograph (photo_adler.jpg, 500x667) that is too tall on the phone. The executor reported the same and stopped, because the fix needs a new page name. Its page tests (9.37.0: 406 features passed; 9.34.0: 380) and the chapter check Page/Ch11 passed on v9_95_0; the story-layout rule is part of the criterion, so the task is not Done. REPAIR INSIDE THE TASK (the pattern of the chapter 1 and 2 portrait crops; the task stays InProgress and ranks first, ahead of the page build of chapter 12 and the research of chapter 11, which wait for the controlled new page): a landscape head-and-shoulders crop of the Adler photograph as a NEW asset (the original stays), a NEW story-pictures file stories_img_v2_1_0.json that names it, and the page as a NEW file v9_96_0 built with the same template, builder and data builders; v9_95_0 stays as committed. Then page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0, the story-layout probe on EVERY story at the three viewports, the chapter check Page/Ch11 on v9_96_0. The data module of the research (stories v1_0_0) is behind the stories v1_0_1 the page now uses: the research task must read stories v1_0_1 (Multics story without a 56-year span; zlib 'where' over the internet, first built for the libpng image library). The YouTube link z0gguhEmWiY answered 429 on the watch page and 200 on oEmbed: kept." .

ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck14 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 14 deck (03-materials/ch14/SEN0414_Ch14_ExcelSpreadsheets_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 51 slides, 24 examples, 6 stories, with the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch14/page/chapter_code_ch14_v1_0_0.json; commits e0cb053 and c9b813d of the executor session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch14; the earlier deck 08-tooling/ch14-deck/sen0414_ch14_deck_v1_0_0.pptx stays as committed): the controller's own re-runs with the control script sen0414_control_iter20_deck_v1_2_0.py - the deck standard check v1_0_0 prints SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 including M1 (24 of 24), the overlap check ends CLEAN, the first-line error scan of the manifest ends PASS, the 24 examples run now in a fresh interpreter (Python 3.13.16 with openpyxl 3.1.5) print exactly the recorded result, no committed file of the chapter is modified since the Iteration 20 planning commit (23 files added), everything is committed, the 6 story pictures cover the 6 story slides with a licence record. Pyodide: the executor's own Pyodide run dated from an earlier build; the controller repeated it on the FINAL manifest with the executor's runner manifest_pyodide_check_v2_0_0.py and the controller's own installation of pyodide 0.28.2 (Python 3.13.2, openpyxl 3.1.5 and et_xmlfile 2.0.0 from the page's own wheels): 24 examples PASS (log pyodide_ch14.log); the runner is the executor's, the interpreter and the manifest are the controller's. All 15 hyperlinks answered 200. The controller rendered all 51 slides and read the six story slides: 5N1K in each, a READ link in each. Stand-in pictures, judged under the owner's rule (real pictures, not invented ones): only the VisiCalc story shows its person (Dan Bricklin, CC BY 2.0); the OOXML story shows the ISO vote protest of 9 April 2008 (CC BY-SA 2.0), the openpyxl story the project logo enlarged 4x (stated on the slide), the gene-name story panel b of the paper's figure (CC BY 4.0), the Macintosh story a real Macintosh running Excel 1.0 (CC BY 2.0), the Herndon story the title page of the Reinhart and Rogoff working paper (CC BY 2.0). Each is a real picture with a licence and an honest caption saying what it shows, none is drawn or invented, so the deck is accepted; that four stories show the subject and not the named person is an OPEN OWNER CONTENT DECISION recorded beside chapters 2 and 13 (replace with portraits once Wikimedia or another source with a free licence answers). Disclosures of the executor, judged: the examples were run with /usr/bin/python3 because /root/.local/bin/python3.13 lacks openpyxl - the controller's run uses the same interpreter and prints the same results; the census and produce workbooks are in-memory stand-ins said on the slides - accepted; the read_only chart uses the research figures (114 MB against 11 MB), labelled as not a run - accepted. Research/Ch14 was not run by the executor and belongs to the research task (the earlier measurement: environment-dependent claims, 2 mismatches). The page test and story probe belong to the page task."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit ;
