ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck15 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 15 deck (03-materials/ch15/SEN0414_Ch15_GoogleSheets_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 53 slides, 25 examples, 5 native charts, 5 stories, with the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch15/page/chapter_code_ch15_v1_0_0.json and its library block; commit a3ff533 of the executor session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch15; the earlier deck 08-tooling/ch15-deck/sen0414_ch15_deck_v1_0_0.pptx stays as committed): the controller's own re-runs with the control script sen0414_control_iter20_deck_v1_3_0.py - the deck standard check v1_0_0 prints SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 including M1 (25 of 25), the overlap check ends CLEAN, the first-line error scan of the manifest ends PASS, the 14 wheels and the stand-in module named in the manifest's library block match their recorded SHA-256, and the 25 examples run now in ONE interpreter in manifest order (Python 3.13.16, ezsheets 2026.4.28 and the Google client libraries unpacked from those wheels, google_standin) print exactly the recorded result; no committed file of the chapter is modified since the Iteration 20 planning commit (23 files added), everything is committed, the 5 story pictures cover the 5 story slides with a licence record. A first run of control v1_2_0 failed all examples but one because the examples need the wheels; the control script was extended as a new file (v1_3_0), the failed log is not a verdict on the deck. Pyodide: the controller repeated the run with the executor's runner manifest_pyodide_check_v2_0_0.py and the controller's own installation of pyodide 0.28.2 (Python 3.13.2): 25 examples PASS (log pyodide_ch15.log; the runner needs the Pyodide package CDN, which answered). All 16 hyperlinks answered 200. The controller rendered all 53 slides and read the five story slides: 5N1K in each, a READ link in each. Pictures judged under the owner's rule (real pictures, not invented ones; prefer the named person): Rochelle (Flickr, CC BY 2.0) and Cook (CC BY 2.0) are the named people; the Nakamoto story shows the first page of the Bitcoin paper (CC BY 4.0), the Sheets API and Forms stories show Flickr screenshots (Wesley Fryer, CC BY 2.0) of the pages the stories name, not Google product pages: each is a real, licensed picture with an honest caption - accepted; that three stories do not show their person is an OPEN OWNER CONTENT DECISION beside chapters 2, 13 and 14. THE MISSING SIXTH STORY (EzsheetsRelease2019, Al Sweigart): no picture of Sweigart or of EZSheets was reachable, so the deck has five stories, not six. The deck standard asks every story slide to be complete (D5 5 of 5) and does not fix the number, so this is not a gate failure; it is a content gap against the chapter's story list and it is said openly here: it is closed by a later change item (a Deck_Fix by the change route) when a real picture is reachable; the page task of chapter 15 shows the same five stories, so deck and page agree. Disclosures of the executor, judged: Google is never reached - every spreadsheet result comes from the real ezsheets and google-api-python-client talking to google_standin, a stand-in at the HTTP layer, said on the slides and in the manifest - accepted as the only way to run the examples offline; the stand-in has a speed patch (prettyPrintSchema and ByName no-ops) and a new uninstall(), which the later page task must install together with the ch15 wheels (page_data v2.25.0 reads only the examples) - carried to the page task; the quota example was changed after it began with 'HttpError' (error-first rule) - accepted. Research/Ch15: the chapter check FAILS on the execution checks (No module named ezsheets under the system Python) - that is the research task's, to be run under the venv that has ezsheets, or reproduced by an environment the data module builds itself. The page test and story probe belong to the page task."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "deck15" ; backlog:hasTestSpec "08-tooling/sen0414_control_iter20_deck_v1_3_0.py" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "python3 08-tooling/sen0414_control_iter20_deck_v1_3_0.py deck15 exited 0" ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0 with the course repository as workspace" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-25T15:01:19"^^xsd:dateTime .
