helle (Flickr, CC BY 2.0) and Cook (CC BY 2.0) are the named people; the Nakamoto story shows the first page of the Bitcoin paper (CC BY 4.0), the Sheets API and Forms stories show Flickr screenshots (Wesley Fryer, CC BY 2.0) of the pages the stories name, not Google product pages: each is a real, licensed picture with an honest caption - accepted; that three stories do not show their person is an OPEN OWNER CONTENT DECISION beside chapters 2, 13 and 14. THE MISSING SIXTH STORY (EzsheetsRelease2019, Al Sweigart): no picture of Sweigart or of EZSheets was reachable, so the deck has five stories, not six. The deck standard asks every story slide to be complete (D5 5 of 5) and does not fix the number, so this is not a gate failure; it is a content gap against the chapter's story list and it is said openly here: it is closed by a later change item (a Deck_Fix by the change route) when a real picture is reachable; the page task of chapter 15 shows the same five stories, so deck and page agree. Disclosures of the executor, judged: Google is never reached - every spreadsheet result comes from the real ezsheets and google-api-python-client talking to google_standin, a stand-in at the HTTP layer, said on the slides and in the manifest - accepted as the only way to run the examples offline; the stand-in has a speed patch (prettyPrintSchema and ByName no-ops) and a new uninstall(), which the later page task must install together with the ch15 wheels (page_data v2.25.0 reads only the examples) - carried to the page task; the quota example was changed after it began with 'HttpError' (error-first rule) - accepted. Research/Ch15: the chapter check FAILS on the execution checks (No module named ezsheets under the system Python) - that is the research task's, to be run under the venv that has ezsheets, or reproduced by an environment the data module builds itself. The page test and story probe belong to the page task.. Evidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck15, verified by backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0." .
