ex:TK_Ret_Ch16_Deck_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "NOT MET on the first report, found by the controller on 2026-10-26T05:32:40 UTC while reading the story slides of deck v2_0_0 (controller's own re-runs: standard check 13/0/0, M1 25 of 25, overlap clean, 25 examples equal, Pyodide 25 PASS, links 200 except one publisher page that blocks scripts; logs deck16.log, pyodide_ch16.log): slide 25 (the Bobby Tables story, WHO Randall Munroe) shows a crumpled sheet of paper with typed speech text, and the caption says 'Randall Munroe, author of xkcd. Photo: gruntzooki', and story_images_v2_0_0.json says ImageDescription 'Randall Munroe, author of xkcd, accepting a Hugo Award'. The Flickr file is titled 'Randall Munroe's Hugo acceptance speech' and shows the NOTE his speech was read from, not the person; the executor disclosed it as a photo of Munroe. A caption that says a picture shows a person it does not show breaks the owner's rule of real pictures with honest attribution. REPAIR INSIDE THE TASK (the task stays InProgress and ranks first among the chapter 16 tasks): (a) prefer the named person: find a real, freely licensed photograph of Randall Munroe himself (Openverse search, the executor's own fetch script, every helper script committed) and use it with its licence record; (b) only if none is reachable, correct the caption on the slide and the record to say what the picture shows ('The speech note read for Randall Munroe at the 2014 Hugo Awards, Loncon 3. Photo: gruntzooki, CC BY-SA 2.0') and say openly that the story shows no portrait. Also check every other caption of the six stories against what its picture really shows (the controller read slides 6, 8, 12, 30 and 40 and found them honest: Hipp, van Rossum, the SQLite banner, Jim Gray named as the person the researchers built on, Codd). The NEW files: deck SEN0414_Ch16_SQLiteDatabases_3e_v2_0_1.pptx and manifest chapter_code_ch16_v1_0_1.json (the manifest names the deck), a new story_images_v2_0_1.json, the generator as new versions; v2_0_0 stays as committed. Then the standard check, overlap, error-first scan, the examples in a fresh interpreter, the Pyodide run, the links, and the controller's checks." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch10_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "CORRECTION of the control of the chapter 10 page (register 2.242.0), made on 2026-10-26T05:32:40 UTC: that control cited 'the chapter check Page/Ch10 run by the controller under the lock: PASS' as a test of the new page; the committed chapter check calls the page-test runner v1_0_0, whose default page is v9_28_0, so that run tested the EARLIER page v9_28_0, not v9_95_0. The evidence for v9_95_0 is the controller's direct runs of page tests 9.37.0 (402 features, 0 failed) and 9.34.0 (376 features, 0 failed) and the story-layout probe on v9_95_0, all recorded; the verdict stands. A new tool sen0414_lineage_chapter_check_v1_2_0.py (register 2.256.0) tests the newest page and prints the version; the controller re-runs Page/Ch10 with it when the research task of chapter 10 is next touched." .

