ex:TK_Ret_Ch12_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "NOT MET on the first report, found by the controller on 2026-10-26T08:50:47 UTC with its own run of the story-layout probe v1_0_0 under the lock on page v9_95_0 (log 08-tooling/control-iter20-logs/probe_ch12_v9_95_0.log): 'FAIL story 1 at 1366x768: photo height 524 of 768, first text 841.7'; 'FAIL story 1 at 390x844: photo 459 of 844, first text 863.8'; 'FAIL story 2 at 390x844: photo 425 of 844, first text 863.3'; the other probe lines pass. Story 1 is McIlroy and story 2 Ritchie, both portrait photographs. The executor reported the same and stopped (its page tests 9.37.0 400 features and 9.34.0 374 features passed, and Page/Ch12 with the chapter check v1_2_0 printed 'PAGE TESTED v9_95_0' and PASS); the story-layout rule is part of the criterion, so the task is not Done. The controller did not run the page tests on v9_95_0: the page is superseded by the repair. REPAIR INSIDE THE TASK (the pattern of the chapter 1, 2 and 11 portrait crops; the task stays InProgress and ranks first, ahead of the chapter 12 research): crop the McIlroy and Ritchie photographs to landscape head-and-shoulders as NEW assets (the originals stay), a NEW story-pictures file stories_img_v2_1_0.json that names them, and the page as a NEW file v9_96_0 built with the same template, builder and data builders; v9_95_0 stays as committed. Then page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the lock, the story-layout probe on EVERY story at the three viewports (the picture crop must also keep stories 3 and 4 passing), the chapter check Page/Ch12 with v1_2_0 (it prints the page version tested: it must say v9_96_0). The result file: the runner v1_1_0 ignores the RESULTS environment variable and writes results.json into its own /tmp/page_test_* folder, so copy that file into the repository as test_results_v9_96_0.json (08-tooling/ch12-page) after each run. The ch12 deck pictures stay as they are (the McIlroy and Ritchie credit, one artist for both, is still not independently verified by the controller)." .

