ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck17 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Control by the lineage agent: the chapter 17 deck (03-materials/ch17/SEN0414_Ch17_PDFAndWordDocuments_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 58 slides, 28 examples, 5 stories, with the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch17/page/chapter_code_ch17_v1_0_0.json; commits 1995502 and 6a29f66 of the executor session SEN0414-I20-deck-ch17; the earlier deck 08-tooling/ch17-deck/sen0414_ch17_deck_v1_0_0.pptx stays as committed): the controller's own re-runs with the control script sen0414_control_iter20_deck_v1_4_0.py - the deck standard check prints SUMMARY PASS=13 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 including M1 (28 of 28), the overlap check ends CLEAN, the first-line error scan of the manifest ends PASS, the 28 examples run now in a fresh interpreter (Python 3.13.16) print exactly the recorded result, no committed file of the chapter is modified since the planning commit (29 files added), everything is committed, the 5 story pictures cover the 5 story slides with a licence record in ASSETS_PROVENANCE_v1_0_0.md and story_images_v2_0_0.json. Pyodide: the controller repeated the run with the executor's runner on the controller's own pyodide 0.28.2 installation: Python 3.13.2 with pypdf 6.20.1, python-docx 1.2.0 and the other wheels, 28 examples PASS (log pyodide_ch17.log). All 16 hyperlinks answered 200. The controller rendered all 58 slides and read the five story slides: 5N1K in each, a READ link in each. CAPTIONS CHECKED against what each picture shows (the rule found on chapter 16): Warnock - a portrait of John Warnock, caption names him; PDF standard - Adobe's headquarters towers, the caption says so and the WHO line names Adobe Systems and the ISO committee; ZIP - a PKZIP floppy disk, the caption says 'A PKZIP floppy disk, label of PKWARE' and does not say it shows Phil Katz; docx standard - boxes of Microsoft Office 2007 on a shop shelf, said so; the python-docx story - the Python Package Index home page of 6 December 2007 in a screenshot, said so (it is not the docx page of the story, and the caption does not say it is). Each caption names only what its picture shows, so the deck is accepted; that three of the five stories show an object and not the person is an OPEN OWNER CONTENT DECISION beside chapters 2, 13, 14 and 15 (replace with portraits when a free source is reachable). Disclosures of the executor, judged: stand-in files instead of the book's files, named on the slides - accepted; the Adobe headquarters picture is a Wikimedia thumbnail taken after a 429 - accepted, real picture with its licence; Research/Ch17 not run by the executor - belongs to the research task (the earlier measurement: environment-dependent claims, 4 mismatches). The page test and story probe belong to the page task."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC2F_Retrofit ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "deck17" ; backlog:hasTestSpec "08-tooling/sen0414_control_iter20_deck_v1_4_0.py" ;
