ex:TK_Ret_Ch14_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "NOT MET on the first report (2026-10-26T12:07:52 UTC; the controller's own run of 9.37.0 on v9_95_0 is queued behind the shared lock and its result is added as a later note; the executor's committed logs in 08-tooling/ch14-page/logs_iter20 are the evidence meanwhile): page v9_95_0 of chapter 14, page tests 9.37.0: 394 features passed, 8 FAILED; 9.34.0: 368 passed, 8 FAILED; chapter check Page/Ch14 FAIL with 'PAGE TESTED v9_95_0'. Passed: manifest scan (24 examples, 0 errors), story probe 18 of 18, chapter-code consistency, P1 to P9, P11, P12. CAUSE (deterministic, found by the executor): the recorded results of the page's observed programs (interpreter_record_v1_0_0.json, live_observations_v1_0_0.json, page_data) were recorded with Python 3.14.6, the browser runs Pyodide 0.28.2 (Python 3.13): ElementTree writes '<col ... />' where the record has '<col .../>', and a cached-value example gives (500, None) where the record has (None, None); the widgets w-CachedValueLoss and w-HidingRowsColumns fail and the failure cascades to the Lab and exercise counts. The deck is not at fault: its 24 examples were recorded and re-run under Python 3.13 and under Pyodide (controller's run: 24 of 24 PASS). Other pages: chapters 10 (406/380), 11 and 12 (400/374) pass, so this is specific to chapter 14, whose page observes programs that depend on the interpreter's library versions. REPAIR INSIDE THE TASK (the task stays InProgress and ranks first; the chapter 14 research waits for the controlled new page): record the expected results of every observed program of the page with an interpreter that behaves like the page's runtime - the Pyodide 0.28.2 run itself (the executor's runner 08-tooling/ch14-deck/manifest_pyodide_check_v2_0_0.py and pyodide_probe_v2_0_0.js show how; the chapter 14 wheels are in 03-materials/ch14/assets) - as NEW record files (interpreter_record_v1_1_0.json and any other new version the builder needs; page-data builder as a new version file if it must read them), rebuild as the NEW page v9_96_0 (v9_95_0 stays as committed), then page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0 under the lock (all features pass, none skipped), the story probe on every story at the three viewports, the chapter check Page/Ch14 with v1_2_0 (it must print v9_96_0), copy results.json into the repository as test_results_v9_96_0.json, and say which values changed and why. The runner v1_1_0 ignores RESULTS and writes results.json into its /tmp/page_test_* folder." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch15_Page_Build backlog:hasAuditNote "FORWARD NOTE from the chapter 14 page failure (2026-10-26T12:07:52 UTC): a page that shows the recorded result of a program must record it with the interpreter the page runs on, Pyodide 0.28.2 (Python 3.13), not with the build machine's Python 3.14: ElementTree output, library versions and cached values differ. Before the page build: run every observed program and every example through the Pyodide runner of the chapter's deck (manifest_pyodide_check_v2_0_0.py) and record the page's expected results from that run; after the build: page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.0, probe, Page/ChNN with chapter check v1_2_0 (it prints the page version tested)." .
